      "comment" : "What VoiceOver calls the feed downloads section's bar, which counts every download of the run."
    },
    "All levels" : {
      "comment" : "Choice of the headings sheet's level filter that shows every level."
    },
    "All subfolders now sorted by %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver announcement after the sort is applied to every subfolder. %@ is the sort, such as \"Title, ascending\"."
    },
    "Already at the end." : {
      "comment" : "Said when a step forward in the audio editor can go no further."
    },
    "Already at the start." : {
      "comment" : "Said when a step back in the audio editor can go no further."
    },
    "Already in Library" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the library's alert as a ZIP batch that found books but added none, because the library already held every one. Title case."
    },
    "Also write the markers as Audacity labels" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the checkbox in the audio editor's Export Audio sheet that writes the markers as a label file too. Audacity is the name of an audio editing program."
    },
    "Also write to the library's copy of the EPUB file" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the metadata editor's switch that also writes the edited title, author, publisher and date into the library's own copy of the book's EPUB file."
    },
    "Always" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). A visibility as the Visibility pop-up names it: \"Always\", \"When Applicable\", or \"Hidden\". This is the case .always."
    },
    "Always offers a view all the time. When Applicable offers it only while it lists something: the Reading List while it holds a book, episode, or article, and Feeds while there is a feed. Hidden leaves it out. A window keeps its view until you choose another." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What the three visibilities do, and that a window keeps its view."
    },
    "Ampersand" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"&\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Ampersand\"."
    },
    "An article's details come from its feed; %@ makes it a book you can edit." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the heading of an article's read-only Book Information sheet: why nothing can be changed, and the way out. %@ is the name of the Move to Library command."
    },
    "An e-book with the book's headings, contents, and any page numbers, for Apple Books and other reading apps. It holds no pictures." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Convert to picker in the Export dialog while EPUB is chosen. Apple Books is an app's name."
    },
    "An edit of its text is kept beside the new reading, as a copy in the book's package." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What a re-read does to text TextMouth did not write, said only for a book whose content.md holds such text: an edit made with Edit Text, or a save no edit took, either kept as Replace Existing keeps it (ImportDecisionWording.replacingKeepsTextSentence)."
    },
    "An episode in its feed can't be edited." : {
      "comment" : "Said when Edit Audio… reaches a podcast episode that lives in its feed's folder, which can't be edited."
    },
    "An episode's details come from its feed; %@ makes it a book you can edit." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the heading of an episode's read-only Book Information sheet: why nothing can be changed, and the way out. %@ is the name of the Move to Library command."
    },
    "An option of the %@ filter has a value but no name." : {
      "comment" : "Problem found in a typed filter chain: an equals sign with nothing before it, in one filter's options. %@ is the filter's name, such as volume."
    },
    "An unknown error occurred." : {
      "comment" : "Message of an alert about a problem, when nothing more is known about it."
    },
    "And %lld more copies, which the log lists." : {
      "comment" : "Last paragraph of the report of conflicting copies: how many more copies there are than the report names. %lld is the number of copies.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "And %lld more copy, which the log lists."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "And %lld more copies, which the log lists."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "And %lld more files couldn't be read." : {
      "comment" : "Last line of the list of unread files in Compare Libraries when the list is cut short. %lld is how many more files could not be read, a count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "And %lld more file couldn't be read."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "And %lld more files couldn't be read."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Announce level every %lld seconds" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the switch in the Record window that makes VoiceOver speak the microphone level while recording. %lld is how many seconds pass between announcements.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Announce level every %lld second"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Announce level every %lld seconds"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Another view is already named %@. Choose another name." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. Save's problem with a name another view has. Placeholders in order: name."
    },
    "Another view is named %@. Rename it first, then restore this view." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). What Restore Default says, changing nothing, when another view has the shipped name name (finding 5). Placeholders in order: name."
    },
    "Answer this one when the move ends." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of what an import question says when it is answered while the library is being moved."
    },
    "Any Condition" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A match as its pop-up names it. This is the form for the other case of the condition."
    },
    "Any other book passes over The, A, and An." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the note under the Leading Articles pop-up: the articles skipped for a book in any other language. The, A, and An are the English articles and stay as written."
    },
    "Apostrophe" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"'\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Apostrophe\"."
    },
    "Appends a new step to the gesture sequence" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Add gesture step button in the Miscellaneous settings."
    },
    "Apple Lossless (M4A)" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an audio file format in the audio editor's Export format list and in messages about a save: M4A files holding Apple Lossless audio. Apple Lossless is Apple's name for the codec."
    },
    "Applied %@ to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Said as a filter has been applied to a selection in the audio editor. %1$@ is the filter preset's name and %2$@ the selection's length in words.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Applied %1$@ to %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Applied %@ to all of the audio." : {
      "comment" : "Said as a filter has been applied to the whole audio in the audio editor. %@ is the filter preset's name."
    },
    "Applies only to a view that lists episodes or articles." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. Its hint while the view lists no episodes or articles, when it is dimmed (review of October 31, 2026, finding 6)."
    },
    "Applies the filter." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the audio editor's Apply button while a press applies the filter."
    },
    "Applies the rules to text before it is spoken" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Enable text substitutions switch in the Substitutions settings."
    },
    "Apply" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the Clean Up Transcript sheet that makes the corrections in the transcript.\nButton of the audio editor's Apply Filter sheet that applies the filter."
    },
    "Apply Filter" : {
      "comment" : "Name of an edit, as the Undo and Redo menu items say it after \"Undo\" or \"Redo\"; also the title of the audio editor's filter sheet."
    },
    "Apply Filter lists these in this order. Each is a chain of filters in ffmpeg's syntax, such as highpass=f=80,volume=3dB. TextMouth runs its own filters, plus every ffmpeg filter when ffmpeg is installed and turned on above." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the filter presets sheet. Apply Filter is the audio editor's command. \"highpass=f=80,volume=3dB\" is filter syntax and stays as it is. ffmpeg is the name of a program. \"turned on above\" refers to the Use ffmpeg for filters switch in Storage settings."
    },
    "Apply Filter plays a preview first, and applies when you choose Apply again." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the Preview filters before applying switch in Storage settings. Apply Filter and Apply are the audio editor's command and button."
    },
    "Apply Filter…" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Opens the choice of audio filters to apply to the selection."
    },
    "Apply Sort to All Subfolders" : {
      "comment" : "Item of the Sort menu that gives every subfolder of the folder shown the sort chosen here."
    },
    "Apply to" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the choice in the audio editor's Apply Filter sheet of what to filter: the selection or the whole file."
    },
    "Applying %@." : {
      "comment" : "Said as a filter begins to be applied in the audio editor. %@ is the filter preset's name."
    },
    "Articles" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the count of a feed's articles in Feed Info. Title case.\nText of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A kind of row as its checkbox names it: \"Books\", \"Episodes\", \"Articles\", or \"Feeds\". This is the case .articles."
    },
    "Articles (%lld of %@ listed)" : {
      "comment" : "The heading of a feed's articles when the library lists fewer than the feed has. %lld is how many are listed; %@ is the feed's size, such as \"381\" or \"more than 2000\". Title case.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Articles (%lld of %@ listed)"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Articles (%lld of %@ listed)"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Articles (%lld)" : {
      "comment" : "The header of a list's news articles, with their count: \"Articles (3)\". %lld is the number of articles.\nThe heading of a feed's articles, which counts the rows under it. %lld is how many. Title case.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Articles (%lld)"
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Articles (%lld)"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Artist" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's field for an audiobook's artist."
    },
    "Artist or narrator" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the book information sheet's field for an audiobook's artist, who may be its narrator."
    },
    "As the table defines" : {
      "comment" : "How a braille table contracts, for a table that says neither its contraction nor its grade: it writes as its own rules define."
    },
    "Ascending" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A direction as the pop-up names it. This is the form for the first case of the condition."
    },
    "Ask Each Time" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the After Importing a Book pop-up in the Storage settings: TextMouth asks what to do with the original file after each import."
    },
    "Asks after each audiobook import whether to transcribe it. Off, audiobooks are transcribed only with Transcribe Audio." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the checkbox that offers transcribing after an import. Transcribe Audio is the command's name."
    },
    "Asks before deleting." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the VoiceOver hint of a delete command that asks before it deletes."
    },
    "Asks first, then deletes this feed, its downloads, and what it kept of downloads you removed" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Delete Feed button in Feed Info."
    },
    "Asks first, then gives the library a new identity and opens it." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the button that gives the library a new identity file."
    },
    "Asks first, then makes a new library index from the books in this folder and opens the library." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the button that opens the library without its index file."
    },
    "Asks first, then replaces every rule with the defaults." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Reset to Defaults button in the Substitutions settings."
    },
    "Asks first, then stops checking; the feed and its downloads stay" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Unsubscribe button in Feed Info when it asks a question first."
    },
    "Asks first, then writes the identity this Mac knows for the library and opens it." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the button that restores the library's identity file."
    },
    "Asks for an optional note, then marks the reading position." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Bookmarks list's Add Bookmark button: it opens the step where an optional note is written, then the bookmark is added where the book is being read.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Pide una nota opcional y luego marca la posición de lectura."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Asks whether to %@ or keep them in the TextMouth library folder." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Remove button when it asks first. %@ is what deleting the files does, such as \"move the files to the Trash\" or \"delete the files permanently\"."
    },
    "Asterisk" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"*\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Asterisk\"."
    },
    "At Sign" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"@\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + At Sign\"."
    },
    "Attach" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the file panel opened by Attach Transcript, which attaches the chosen file."
    },
    "Attach Transcript" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the alert saying why Attach Transcript did nothing or why the chosen file was not attached."
    },
    "Attach Transcript…" : {
      "comment" : "Menu item that gives an audiobook a transcript from a WebVTT or SubRip file instead of transcribing it. The ellipsis means a file panel follows."
    },
    "Attached from %@ files at import, on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying a transcript came from files found beside the audio when the book was imported. %1$@ is the files' formats, such as \"WebVTT and SubRip\"; %2$@ is a date.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Attached from %1$@ files at import, on %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attached from a %@ file on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying a transcript came from a file the user attached, whose name is not known. %1$@ is the file format's name, such as WebVTT or SubRip; %2$@ is a date.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Attached from a %1$@ file on %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attached from a file on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying a transcript came from a file the user attached, whose name and format are not known. %@ is a date, such as \"October 30, 2026\"."
    },
    "Attached from files at import, on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying a transcript came from files found beside the audio when the book was imported, whose names and formats are not known. %@ is a date."
    },
    "Attached from “%@” at import, on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying a transcript came from a file found beside the audio when the book was imported. %1$@ is the file's name; %2$@ is a date.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Attached from “%1$@” at import, on %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attached from “%@” on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying a transcript came from one file the user attached. %1$@ is the file's name; %2$@ is a date, such as \"October 30, 2026\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Attached from “%1$@” on %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attached on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying when a transcript was attached, when its origin is not known. %@ is a date."
    },
    "Attached “%@” to %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver hears once a transcript file is attached. %1$@ is the file's name; %2$@ is the audiobook's title; %3$@ is the number of words, such as \"7,077 words\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Attached “%1$@” to %2$@: %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Attaching “%@” to %@." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver hears as a transcript file starts to be attached. %1$@ is the file's name; %2$@ is the audiobook's title.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Attaching “%1$@” to %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Audacity labels mark one audio file, and this book's audio is in %lld files." : {
      "comment" : "Why Audacity labels could not be exported, after the file's name in a failure sentence. %lld is the number of audio files the book has, always more than one.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Audacity labels mark one audio file, and this book's audio is in %lld file."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Audacity labels mark one audio file, and this book's audio is in %lld files."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Audio" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book format of an audiobook, a book made of audio files, shown in a book's information, the format column, and the duplicate finder.\nPart of a spoken audio export's file name, after the book's title: the whole book, as in \"Middlemarch - Audio\".\nThe name of the Audio checkbox in the Export dialog: the book's audio."
    },
    "Audio Editing" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the Audio Editing group in Storage settings: what happens to originals of edited audio, ffmpeg, and the audio editor's behaviour."
    },
    "Audio Editor" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group of the audio editor's keyboard shortcuts in Settings."
    },
    "Audio Info" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the audio editor's Audio Info sheet."
    },
    "Audio Info…" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Shows information about the audio, such as its format and length."
    },
    "Audio Settings" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the reader's sheet and toolbar button for an audiobook's own settings (its speed), and what VoiceOver calls that button."
    },
    "Audio Speed" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group in an audiobook's own settings sheet that holds its speed."
    },
    "Audio speed" : {
      "comment" : "Label of an audiobook's speed slider; VoiceOver reads it before the speed."
    },
    "Audio that TextMouth converts at import keeps only the converted file." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Keep Originals switch while it is off."
    },
    "Audio: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Transcribe Audio sheet giving the audiobook's length. %@ is the length in words, such as \"6 hours, 12 minutes, 4 seconds\"."
    },
    "Audio: length not known yet." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Transcribe Audio sheet before the audiobook's length is known."
    },
    "Audiobook Loudness" : {
      "comment" : "Title of a premade audio filter preset: sets the whole audio's loudness to a level for audiobooks."
    },
    "Author" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a way to sort the books: by the author. Shown in the Sort menu, the library view editor, the window title, and in sort announcements.\nName of the book information sheet's field for a book's author; VoiceOver reads it as the field's label."
    },
    "Author:" : {
      "comment" : "Caption beside the author field of the New Book from Text sheet. VoiceOver skips it; the field has its own label."
    },
    "Auto-play after navigation" : {
      "comment" : "Title and VoiceOver label of the checkbox in the Playback settings that starts playing after a jump to a heading, bookmark, or search result."
    },
    "Automatic" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the Text Encoding pop-up's first option, which reads the file again the way an import does, by guessing its encoding."
    },
    "Automatically start playing when you navigate to a heading, bookmark, or search result." : {
      "comment" : "Explanation under the Auto-play after navigation checkbox in the Playback settings."
    },
    "Available only while this feed's articles go on to another article when one ends" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the dimmed Open the next article in pop-up button in a news feed's Feed Info: when it can be used.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Disponible solo mientras los artículos de este canal pasan a otro artículo al terminar uno"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Available only while this feed's episodes go on to another episode when one ends" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the dimmed Open the next episode in pop-up button in a podcast feed's Feed Info: when it can be used.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Disponible solo mientras los episodios de este canal pasan a otro episodio al terminar uno"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Available only while this feed's items go on to another item when one ends" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the dimmed Open the next item in pop-up button in a feed's Feed Info: when it can be used.",
      "localizations" : {
