    },
    "Is Not" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the first case of the condition."
    },
    "It" : {
      "comment" : "The subject of a refusal when the book is named elsewhere, as in a list of books \"Title: It is open in a reader. Close it, then try again.\" Capitalized, as it starts a sentence."
    },
    "It also deletes %@." : {
      "comment" : "The last sentence of the confirmation before Unsubscribe: what else it deletes. %@ is what the feed kept for removed downloads, such as \"the places and bookmarks kept for 3 removed downloads\"."
    },
    "It appears again if the problem returns after it clears." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the VoiceOver hint of the failure banner's Dismiss button."
    },
    "It belongs to its feed while it is downloaded. %@ removes its file and keeps its place and bookmarks." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed episode's book cannot be removed from the library: it belongs to its feed. %@ is the name of the Delete Download command, which the sentence recommends."
    },
    "It can be downloaded again." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says after Delete Download deleted a download that kept nothing of the listener's: the item can be downloaded again."
    },
    "It can be read again now. Choose Try Again to use it." : {
      "comment" : "Why Rebuild Library Index replaced nothing: the library index can be read again. It follows the sentence \"The library index was not rebuilt.\", so \"It\" is the index. Try Again is a button name."
    },
    "It cannot be recovered." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the confirmation about the original file of a book just imported, and the hint of its Delete Permanently button: the file is gone for good."
    },
    "It could not be copied into the library." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a book could not move into the current library format. \"It\" is the book's original file."
    },
    "It couldn't be read." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the report of a conflicting copy: the copy's file could not be read. \"It\" is the copy."
    },
    "It deletes %@: it goes to the Trash, where you can recover it until the Trash is emptied." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, when files go to the Trash: what the feed deletes, one thing. %@ is what is deleted."
    },
    "It deletes %@: it is deleted permanently and cannot be recovered." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, when files are deleted permanently: what the feed deletes, one thing. %@ is what is deleted."
    },
    "It deletes %@: it stays in the TextMouth library folder." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, when the setting keeps files: what the feed deletes, one thing, which stays in the library folder. %@ is what is deleted."
    },
    "It deletes %@: they are deleted permanently and cannot be recovered." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, when files are deleted permanently: what the feed deletes, several things. %@ is a list of what is deleted."
    },
    "It deletes %@: they go to the Trash, where you can recover them until the Trash is emptied." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, when files go to the Trash: what the feed deletes, several things. %@ is a list of what is deleted."
    },
    "It deletes %@: they stay in the TextMouth library folder." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, when the setting keeps files: what the feed deletes, several things, which stay in the library folder. %@ is a list of what is deleted."
    },
    "It has a page list, and the start of each page is marked in the text." : {
