      "comment" : "Name of the book format of a Kindle book in the MOBI format (MOBI is a format name), shown in a book's information, the format column, and the duplicate finder."
    },
    "Label %@" : {
      "comment" : "Heading made at import for an Audacity label that has no text. %@ is the label's place among the file's labels, from 1, an identifier written without digit grouping."
    },
    "Labels and semicolons need ffmpeg. TextMouth's own filters take one comma-separated chain." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said of a filter graph with labels or semicolons, which only the ffmpeg program runs: TextMouth's own filters take a chain separated by commas."
    },
    "Language" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's row that shows the language a book is written in.\nThe label of the pop-up that chooses the language of a braille code, in the Braille tab of Settings and in the Export dialog's braille options.\nTitle of the pop-up in the Voice settings that narrows the voices to one language, and the label of the selected voice's language beneath it.\nTitle of the voice sheet's menu that limits the voices listed to one language."
    },
    "Language: %@" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says for the book information sheet's language row. %@ is the language code the book gives, such as en."
    },
    "Language: %@, %@." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Transcribe Audio sheet naming the transcription language and whether its speech model is ready. %1$@ is the language's name, such as \"English (United States)\"; %2$@ is its status: installed, needs download, downloading, or not supported.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Language: %1$@, %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Last Opened" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a way to sort the books: by the date the book was last opened. Shown in the Sort menu, the library view editor, the window title, and in sort announcements.\nName of the book information sheet's row that shows the date the book was last opened."
    },
    "Last attempt" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the outcome of the last Try Again or Rebuild Library Index, on the library index recovery sheet."
    },
    "Last check" : {
      "comment" : "Label of when the feed was last checked, in Feed Info."
    },
    "Last check failed: %@" : {
      "comment" : "How a feed's last check reads when it failed. %@ is the reason, a sentence, such as \"This Mac is offline, so Planet Money can't be refreshed.\" Spoken after a comma with its first letter in lower case."
    },
    "Last message" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the audio editor's line that repeats the last announcement, so a braille display can read it again."
    },
    "Last opened" : {
      "comment" : "Label of when a book was last opened, in its read-only Book Information sheet."
    },
    "Last opened %@" : {
      "comment" : "Speak Info: the part of a book's full summary that says when it was last opened. %@ is a date or time, such as \"yesterday\"."
    },
    "Last try: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Text below the Try a Double Press button after a trial ended. %@ is what the trial found, a whole sentence such as \"Double press.\"."
    },
    "Leading articles" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up in the Library settings that chooses whether a title's leading article (The, A, An) counts when sorting and typing."
    },
    "Leaves the audiobook untranscribed; Transcribe Audio does it later." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Not Now button of the question offered after an import. Transcribe Audio is the command's name."
