    },
    "Nothing Imported" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the library's alert as a ZIP batch that brought no new book ends. Nothing failed, so it is no error. Title case."
    },
    "Nothing checks that this is the right choice. If numbers and punctuation sound wrong, choose another." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What the alert says first of a choice between two seven-bit codes: nothing can tell whether it is right, since every printable ASCII byte is a cell in every seven-bit code, so a wrong one reads with no error (research of October 25, section 8.3)."
    },
    "Nothing could be compared with the copy in %@, because a file the comparison needs couldn't be read." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the results of Compare Libraries when the other copy's library index could not be read. %@ is the other copy's folder path."
    },
    "Nothing has been cut or copied." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the audio editor's Paste when nothing has been cut or copied."
    },
    "Nothing is changed." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of what the Compare Libraries sheet says while it works: the comparison changes nothing in either copy."
    },
    "Nothing is copied, and nothing is created in %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the question asked before using another library while the one in use is not available. %@ is the path of the library in use."
    },
    "Nothing is copied, and the library in %@ stays as it is." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the question asked before using another library. %@ is the path of the library in use."
    },
    "Nothing is created in %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the question asked before starting a new library. %@ is the path of the library in use."
    },
    "Nothing is playing." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor's Stop is pressed with nothing playing."
    },
    "Nothing is selected." : {
      "comment" : "Said when an audio editor command needs a selection and there is none.\nText of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What a press of Speak Info, or of Return (Open Selected Book), says when no row is selected."
    },
    "Nothing matches this view now." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library window's View pop-up and Go to View. The row a view shows while it lists nothing at all: the Feeds view, a view the listener made, and any view without a Books section (LibraryView.showsEmptySentence)."
    },
    "Nothing to revert: no edit can be undone." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the audio editor's Revert to Original when no edit can be undone."
    },
    "Nothing to save: the book's audio holds every edit." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the audio editor's Save when there is nothing to save."
    },
    "Nothing was changed." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of a message that says saving failed: nothing the user edited was saved anywhere.\nLast sentence of a refusal to read a book again: the book and its text are as they were."
    },
    "Nothing was exported." : {
      "comment" : "What an export says once it ends when it wrote nothing."
    },
    "Nothing was recorded, so there is nothing to save." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when the recording was stopped before any audio was captured."
    },
    "Now %@ long." : {
      "comment" : "Ends the announcement of an edit in the audio editor: the audio's new length. %@ is the length in words."
    },
    "Now Reading" : {
      "comment" : "Badge on a book's row in the Library list: the book is open in a reader window now."
    },
    "Number Sign" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the punctuation key \"#\", spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Number Sign\"."
    },
    "OK" : {
      "comment" : "Button that closes a notice.\nButton that closes an alert and changes nothing.\nButton that closes an alert that only informs. Title case.\nButton that dismisses an alert about a problem.\nButton that dismisses an alert after reading it.\nButton that dismisses the reader's error alert.\nTitle of the button that dismisses the alert telling the result of importing or exporting pronunciation rules."
    },
    "Of each feed's episodes and articles, lists only the one you opened last." : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. Its hint."
    },
    "Off" : {
      "comment" : "The word for a setting that is turned off, as a slider's or stepper's value says it, such as the sleep timer's fade out.\nVoiceOver value of the iPhone reader's Sleep Timer button while no sleep timer runs.",
