    },
    "Stops comparing. Nothing in either copy has been changed." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Stop button of the Compare Libraries sheet."
    },
    "Stops every feed download, including those waiting, and deletes what they had downloaded." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says the feed downloads section's Cancel button does: it stops every feed download and deletes what they had downloaded."
    },
    "Stops moving the library. The library stays where it is, and nothing is changed." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the button that cancels the move of the library."
    },
    "Stops playback resuming when headphones disconnect" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Enable Bluetooth monitoring switch in the Miscellaneous settings."
    },
    "Stops playing, and goes back to where playing began." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the audio editor's Stop button."
    },
    "Stops recording and saves it in your library as an audiobook." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Stop button in the Record window."
    },
    "Stops saying the code was guessed. The book is not read again." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts."
    },
    "Stops the download. Nothing is installed." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Cancel Download button."
    },
    "Stops the export and keeps the chapters already spoken until TextMouth quits, a different spoken audio export starts, or the book's voice, text, substitutions, or pauses change. Exporting the same range at the same speed and pitch goes on from them." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Stop button in the Export dialog while a spoken audio export runs."
    },
    "Stops the export. The file being made is not kept." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Stop button in the Export dialog."
    },
    "Stops the import under way and those waiting. Books already imported stay." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the import overlay's Cancel button."
    },
    "Stops the search, keeping the matches found so far" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Stop button of the Search Library window."
    },
    "Stops the whole export. Files already written stay." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Cancel Export button in the alert an export shows when a chapter nests too deeply."
    },
    "Stops transcribing. The book stays as it was." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Cancel button of the Transcribe Audio sheet while transcribing."
    },
    "Stops waiting for the download" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the Cancel button of the reader's view while a book downloads."
    },
    "Storage" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the Settings tab for where the library is stored, importing books, and the logs."
    },
    "Storage Directory" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the first section of Storage settings, about where the library lives."
    },
    "Storage problems" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the banner at the top of the library that lists problems saving or removing files."
    },
    "Subfolders" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Folder Settings sheet, which shows one library folder's facts and its listening options. The label of the folder's own subfolders, shown only when it has any."
    },
    "Subheading" : {
      "comment" : "A unit a skip or navigation picker moves by: one subheading, a heading below the main headings."
    },
    "Subscribe" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the button that subscribes to a feed, in the Add Feed sheet."
    },
    "Subscribe to %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Subscribe button of one podcast in the search results. %@ is the podcast's title."
    },
    "Subscribed" : {
      "comment" : "Label of when the listener subscribed to the feed, in Feed Info.\nText of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the other case of the condition."
    },
    "Subscribed to %@. This feed uses plain http, so others can read or change what it sends; TextMouth still loads it." : {
      "comment" : "The warning shown once after subscribing to a feed whose address uses plain http. %@ is the feed's title."
    },
    "Subscribed to %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says once a subscription is made. The first %@ is the feed's title; the second is the feed's size, such as \"10 of 381 episodes listed\" or \"12 episodes\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Subscribed to %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Subscribed to %lld feeds." : {
      "comment" : "What the Import OPML sheet says once the import ended: how many feeds were subscribed to. %lld is how many.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Subscribed to %lld feed."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Subscribed to %lld feeds."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Subscribes to this podcast and fills the address field" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Subscribe button of one podcast in the search results."
    },
    "Subscribing to %@, %lld of %lld…" : {
      "comment" : "What the Import OPML sheet shows while it subscribes to the feeds. The first %@ is the title of the feed being subscribed to; the first %lld is its number in the file; the second %lld is how many feeds the file lists.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Subscribing to %1$@, %2$lld of %3$lld…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Subscription" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A kind of test as a condition's test pop-up names it. This is the case .subscribed."
    },
    "Subtle" : {
      "comment" : "The name of punctuation pause level 1: only periods pause."
    },
    "Switch to a Library or book window, then choose Export again." : {
      "comment" : "What choosing File, Export says when another window, such as Settings, is in front of the Library and book windows."
    },
    "Switches to jump to page controls" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the status row's page button while the jump to percent or time panel is open."
    },
    "Switches to jump to percent controls" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the reader's percent button while the jump to time or page panel is open."
    },
    "Switches to jump to time controls" : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the reader's time button while the jump to percent or page panel is open."
    },
    "Switching loses the changes TextMouth couldn't save while the library isn't available." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence in the question asked before switching libraries: changes that could not be saved are lost. The failure notices follow."
    },
    "Switching to the library in %@..." : {
      "comment" : "Storage settings status line while TextMouth switches to the library in a chosen folder. %@ is the folder's path."
    },
    "System" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + System\"."
    },
    "System Request" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + System Request\"."
    },
    "Tab" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Tab\"."
    },
    "Take it off the reading list, or clear %@ in the Reading List's options first." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of why Remove Download was refused for a book the reading list keeps downloaded: what to do first. %@ is the name of the Reading List's option that keeps its books downloaded, as the option shows it."
    },
    "Taken from %@" : {
      "comment" : "Announced by VoiceOver after a key was given to a keyboard shortcut action that another action had. %@ names the action or actions that lost the key, such as \"Play / Pause and Where Am I?\"."
    },
    "Takes %lld to %lld minutes." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the sleep timer sheet's custom minutes field on the iPhone: the fewest and most minutes it takes. %1$lld is the fewest (1); %2$lld the most (480).",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Takes %1$lld to %2$lld minutes."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Admite de %1$lld a %2$lld minutos."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes %lld to %lld minutes. Return sets the timer and plays the book." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the sleep timer sheet's custom minutes field on the Mac: the fewest and most minutes it takes, and what the Return key does there. %1$lld is the fewest (1); %2$lld the most (480). Return is the name of the key.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Takes %1$lld to %2$lld minutes. Return sets the timer and plays the book."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Admite de %1$lld a %2$lld minutos. Retorno programa el temporizador y reproduce el libro."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes each finished book off the list when its window moves on or closes. Books finished before you turn it on stay." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Reading List's Remove books when finished checkbox.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Quita de la lista cada libro terminado cuando su ventana pasa a otro libro o se cierra. Los libros terminados antes de activarlo se quedan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Takes the selected books off the reading list. They stay in the library." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Library's edit-mode bar button Remove from Reading List.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Quita los libros seleccionados de la lista de lectura. Siguen en la biblioteca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Test" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the button that tests a substitution rule on the input, and the heading of the group that holds it, in the rule editor."
    },
    "Test input" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the field in the substitution rule editor where text is typed to test the rule on."
    },
    "Test input text" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the test input field in the substitution rule editor."
    },
    "Test result: %@" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the text a substitution rule made of the test input. %@ is the result."
    },
    "Test this rule against the input" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Test button in the substitution rule editor."
    },
    "Text" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the Settings tab for text substitution rules and repeated symbols."
    },
    "Text Encoding" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. The label of Book Information's row, and pop-up, that names the encoding."
    },
    "Text as %@" : {
      "comment" : "The name of a text checkbox in the Export dialog while its text is converted. %@ is the name of the format, such as HTML or RTF."
    },
    "Text as Markdown" : {
      "comment" : "The name of a checkbox in the Export dialog: the book's text written as Markdown."
    },
    "Text as plain text" : {
      "comment" : "The name of a checkbox in the Export dialog: the words TextMouth reads aloud, as plain text."
    },
    "Text as spoken audio" : {
      "comment" : "The name of a checkbox in the Export dialog: the book's text spoken by its voice into one audio file."
    },
    "Text content" : {
      "comment" : "Spoken label of the text area of the New Book from Text sheet."
    },
    "Text encoding: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Speak Info's sentence for an encoding described as description (\"Windows-1251 (Cyrillic), guessed\"): \"Text encoding: Windows-1251 (Cyrillic), guessed\". Placeholders in order: description."
    },
    "Text extraction progress: %lld of %lld" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the progress of Redo Text Extraction. %1$lld is how many books are done; %2$lld is how many books there are.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Text extraction progress: %1$lld of %2$lld"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text not updated: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited text could not be taken for a reason the system or another part of the app gives. %@ is the reason."
    },
    "Text not updated: %@ was removed, or its download deleted, so Edit Text has stopped for it." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an Edit Text session ends because the book left the library. %@ is the book's title. Edit Text is a menu command."
    },
    "Text not updated: chapter %@ of the edited text of %@ %@, which TextMouth can't read safely. Flatten it and save again, or undo the change; the book keeps its old text until then." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited text was refused because one chapter nests lists or quotes too deeply. %1$@ is the chapter's number, an identifier written without digit grouping; %2$@ is the book's title; %3$@ is a clause such as \"nests more than 20 levels deep\", written by another part of the app.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Text not updated: chapter %1$@ of the edited text of %2$@ %3$@, which TextMouth can't read safely. Flatten it and save again, or undo the change; the book keeps its old text until then."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text not updated: the edited text of %@ %@, which TextMouth can't read safely. Flatten it and save again, or undo the change; the book keeps its old text until then." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited text was refused because it nests lists or quotes too deeply. %1$@ is the book's title; %2$@ is a clause such as \"nests more than 20 levels deep\", written by another part of the app.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Text not updated: the edited text of %1$@ %2$@, which TextMouth can't read safely. Flatten it and save again, or undo the change; the book keeps its old text until then."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text not updated: the edited text of %@ has no chapter with any text. Undo the change and save again; the book keeps its old text until then." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited text was refused because no chapter has any text left. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "Text not updated: the edited text of %@ isn't UTF-8 text. Save it as UTF-8; the book keeps its old text until then." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited text was refused because it is not UTF-8 text. %@ is the book's title. UTF-8 is a text encoding."
    },
    "Text not updated: the edited transcript of %@ adds words to a chapter with no speech, where they can't be kept. Remove them and save again; the book keeps its old text until then." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited transcript was refused because the user added words to a chapter with no speech. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "Text not updated: the edited transcript of %@ changes a chapter's heading, which comes from its audio. Put it back and save again; the book keeps its old text until then." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited transcript was refused because the user changed a chapter's heading. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "Text not updated: the edited transcript of %@ has %@, but the audiobook has %@. Keep every line beginning with <!-- chapter: and save again; the book keeps its old text until then." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited transcript was refused because its number of chapters no longer matches the audiobook's. %1$@ is the book's title; %2$@ and %3$@ are counts of chapters such as \"3 chapters\". \"<!-- chapter:\" is literal text in the file and stays exactly as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Text not updated: the edited transcript of %1$@ has %2$@, but the audiobook has %3$@. Keep every line beginning with <!-- chapter: and save again; the book keeps its old text until then."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text not updated: the original file of %@ changed too. The book's text is read from it again the next time the book opens." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited text was not taken because the book's own file changed too. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "Text not updated: the transcript of %@ changed too. The book's text is written from it again the next time the book opens." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when an edited text was not taken because the book's transcript changed too. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "Text recognition could not read %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Warning after a book of pictures was imported: text recognition could not read some pages. %1$@ is how many of how many, such as \"1 of 12 pages\", and %2$@ names the pages and why, such as \"page 3 (its picture could not be decoded)\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Text recognition could not read %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text recognition could not read any of the %lld pages: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book of several pages of pictures was refused at import: text recognition could not read any page. %1$lld is the number of pages and %2$@ names the pages and why, such as \"pages 1 and 2 (its picture could not be decoded)\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Text recognition could not read any of the %lld page: %@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Text recognition could not read any of the %lld pages: %@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Text recognition could not read the only page: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book of one page of a picture was refused at import: text recognition could not read its only page. %@ names the page and why, such as \"page 1 (its picture could not be decoded)\"."
    },
    "Text substitution rules could not be saved: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Failure notice: the text substitution rules could not be saved. %@ is the reason, a sentence from the system."
    },
    "Text substitution rules saved." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after a retry saved the text substitution rules that had failed to save."
    },
    "Text to find in every book" : {
      "comment" : "Placeholder of the empty search field in the Search Library window."
    },
    "Text updated" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after the user saved an edited text and TextMouth took it as the book's text. Written without its full stop."
    },
    "Text updated." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after the user saved an edited text of a feed episode's transcript, followed by a note about where the transcript stays."
    },
    "TextMouth Is Open on Another Mac" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the warning shown when another Mac has this library open too."
    },
    "TextMouth Subscriptions" : {
      "comment" : "The title written into an exported OPML file of subscriptions. Title case."
    },
    "TextMouth attaches WebVTT (.vtt) and SubRip (.srt) files." : {
      "comment" : "Alert explaining why a chosen file was not attached as a transcript. WebVTT and SubRip are subtitle file formats, and .vtt and .srt their file extensions."
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert %@ files because its converter is missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: the converter TextMouth carries is missing from the app, which only a damaged copy is. %@ is the name of the file's format, such as WMA or Matroska. Advice to install the app again follows."
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert the sound of “%@”: it is in a kind of audio it does not read." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: its sound is in a codec TextMouth does not decode. %@ is the file's name."
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert “%@”: its sound changes rate or channels partway through, by more than it can follow." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: its sound changes its sample rate or its number of channels partway through, by more than the converter can follow. %@ is the file's name."
    },
    "TextMouth can't convert “%@”: part of its sound is in one piece too large to decode." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: one frame of its sound holds more samples than TextMouth decodes at once. %@ is the file's name."
    },
    "TextMouth can't play this kind of file (%@)." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed's episode could not be downloaded: the file is of a kind TextMouth does not play. %@ is the file's type or extension, such as audio/x-flac."
    },
    "TextMouth can't read the folder %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why the chosen folder can't be used: it can't be read. %1$@ is the folder's path; %2$@ is the reason in a few words, such as \"permission denied\", with no full stop.\nWhy the library can't be used: its folder can't be read. %1$@ is the folder's path; %2$@ is the reason in a few words, such as \"permission denied\", with no full stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't read the folder %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't read this kind of picture (%@). Save it as a PNG or JPEG, then import that copy." : {
      "comment" : "Why a picture was refused at import: a kind of picture the system knows but TextMouth does not decode. %@ is the system's description of the kind, such as \"DNG image\"."
    },
    "TextMouth can't read “%@” as %@. It may be damaged, or named for another format." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: its bytes are not of the format its name says, or are damaged. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$@ the name of the format its name says, such as WMA or AVI video.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't read “%1$@” as %2$@. It may be damaged, or named for another format."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't use the braille table chosen in Settings, “%@”, so this export starts from %@." : {
      "comment" : "Shown in the Export dialog's braille options when the table chosen in Settings can't be used. %1$@ is that table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the table the export starts from, in words such as \"Unified English Braille, uncontracted\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't use the braille table chosen in Settings, “%1$@”, so this export starts from %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth can't use this Mac's table “%@”: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Announced when one of this Mac's braille tables, just chosen, was refused by its check. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the reason, a clause.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth can't use this Mac's table “%1$@”: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth cannot open copy-protected files." : {
      "comment" : "Advice after the refusal of audio that is locked to a store's own player, such as Audible's .aa and .aax files."
    },
    "TextMouth closed while opening %@, so it wasn't reopened." : {
      "comment" : "Announced at launch after the app closed while it was opening a book. %@ is the book's title, which is not opened again."
    },
    "TextMouth could not check this Mac's braille table “%@”: %@. Try again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a braille translation was refused: one of this Mac's braille tables could not be checked. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the reason, which stays English.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth could not check this Mac's braille table “%1$@”: %2$@. Try again."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not check this Mac's table “%@”: %@. Choose it again to retry." : {
      "comment" : "Announced when one of this Mac's braille tables, just chosen, could not be checked. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the reason, a clause.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth could not check this Mac's table “%1$@”: %2$@. Choose it again to retry."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth could not check whether to move it to the Trash." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book's original was kept: TextMouth could not read the choice about the Trash. \"It\" is the original file."
    },
    "TextMouth could not keep the new copy of “%@”. Choose Cancel to discard the copy, then import the file again." : {
      "comment" : "What the duplicate question says when Keep Both could not take the waiting mark off the new copy. %@ is the new copy's title. \"Cancel\" is the sheet's Cancel button."
    },
    "TextMouth could not make a folder to check it in" : {
      "comment" : "Why the check of a braille table of this Mac could not be made, ending a sentence."
    },
    "TextMouth could not move %@ to the current library format." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the alert about books that could not move into the current library format. %@ is a count of books, such as \"3 books\"."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read its library index, the file that records your folders, sort settings, and the order of your books." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the library index recovery sheet: what the unreadable file holds."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the cue sheet “%@”, so its headings were not used." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a cue sheet of an imported folder or archive was not used, because it could not be read. %@ is the cue sheet's name."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the label file “%@”, so its headings were not used." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that an Audacity label file of an imported folder or archive was not used, because it could not be read. %@ is the label file's name."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the reading list in the previous index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the outcome of saving a rebuilt library index: the reading list could not be kept from the old index."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the reading list in the unreadable index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the library index recovery sheet: the reading list could not be read from the unreadable index."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the reading list or the sort settings in the previous index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the outcome of saving a rebuilt library index: neither the reading list nor the sort settings could be kept from the old index."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the reading list or the sort settings in the unreadable index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the library index recovery sheet: neither the reading list nor the sort settings could be read from the unreadable index."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the sort settings in the previous index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the outcome of saving a rebuilt library index: the sort settings could not be kept from the old index."
    },
    "TextMouth could not read the sort settings in the unreadable index." : {
      "comment" : "Part of the library index recovery sheet: the sort settings could not be read from the unreadable index."
    },
    "TextMouth could not record the removal in its package, %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the error shown when Remove from Library Only cannot mark the book's package, so the book stays in the library. %@ is the package's folder name. The sentence that says why follows it."
    },
    "TextMouth could not save a copy of %@, so it left that file unchanged." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why Rebuild Library Index replaced nothing. %@ is the file's path."
    },
    "TextMouth could not save a copy of the unreadable file." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the library index recovery sheet when no copy of the unreadable file was saved."
    },
    "TextMouth could not translate this braille." : {
      "comment" : "Why a braille translation failed, when no more is known."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't get the library's files from %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the library can't be used: fetching its files from the cloud failed. %@ is the cloud service's name, or \"the cloud\" when it is unknown."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't keep the earlier text beside the new download, so the article stays as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed article's new download failed: its earlier text could not be kept beside it."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't keep the edited text of the copy in your library beside the new copy's text, so it left both copies as they are." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when Replace Existing could not keep the edited text of the library's copy beside the new copy's text. Nothing was replaced."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't keep the text you changed in “%@” beside the new reading, so it left the book as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why the book titled bookTitle was not read again: the text changed with Edit Text could not be kept beside the new reading, so nothing was replaced, as Replace Existing leaves both copies then (DuplicateReplacement.TextNotKept). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't make a folder for this feed." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe could not make the feed's folder, when no better reason is known."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't open %@ in Finder." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under the Show Logs in Finder button when Finder could not open the folder. %@ is the folder's full path, which stays as written."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't read %lld files, so this may be incomplete." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of Use This Library's account: some files could not be read. %lld is how many files, a count.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth couldn't read %lld file, so this may be incomplete."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth couldn't read %lld files, so this may be incomplete."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't read “%@” again, so it left the book as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book was not read again with another encoding or braille code: the reading failed. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't read “%@” again, so it left the book as it was: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Why a book was not read again with another encoding or braille code: the reading failed. %1$@ is the book's title and %2$@ is the reason in English, as the reader worded it.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth couldn't read “%1$@” again, so it left the book as it was: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't save its list of this feed's downloads, so the download was kept. Try again once the library can be saved." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed episode's download could not be deleted: the list of the feed's downloads could not be saved."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't save the feed's list of its items, so nothing moved." : {
      "comment" : "Why Move to Library did nothing: the feed's record could not be saved. Follows \"Could not move to the library: \"."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't save the library before deleting the feed “%@”, so nothing was deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Why Delete Feed did nothing: the library could not be saved first. %@ is the feed's title."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't save the library's index, so it left both copies as they are." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when Replace Existing could not save the library's index, which must name the new copy before the old one goes. Nothing was replaced."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't start recording from %@." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when recording from the chosen microphone failed to start. %@ is the microphone's name."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't tell which copy is newer (%@)." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of Use This Library's account when the comparison could not be made. %@ is the reason in English."
    },
    "TextMouth couldn't tell which copy is newer." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of Use This Library's account when the comparison could not be made and no reason is known."
    },
    "TextMouth does not have permission to read the file." : {
      "comment" : "Why the library index could not be loaded: macOS refused TextMouth permission to read it."
    },
    "TextMouth does not open RAR archives. Unpack them, then import what they hold." : {
      "comment" : "Advice after the refusal of a RAR archive that is no comic."
    },
    "TextMouth doesn't read chapter markers back from %@ files, so this book won't list its %lld chapter markers once saved." : {
      "comment" : "Said when a save writes the book's file in a format whose chapter markers TextMouth writes but never reads back as the book's chapters. %1$@ is the format's name, such as \"CAF\", and %2$lld the number of chapter markers.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth doesn't read chapter markers back from %@ files, so this book won't list its chapter marker once saved."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth doesn't read chapter markers back from %@ files, so this book won't list its %lld chapter markers once saved."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth downloads %lld of them again at their feeds' next checks, or the next time it opens." : {
      "comment" : "After Cancel stops feed downloads, several of which TextMouth downloads again by itself. %lld is how many of them it downloads again.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth downloads %lld of them again at their feeds' next checks, or the next time it opens."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth downloads %lld of them again at their feeds' next checks, or the next time it opens."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth downloads 1 of them again at its feed's next check, or the next time it opens." : {
      "comment" : "After Cancel stops feed downloads, exactly one of which TextMouth downloads again by itself."
    },
    "TextMouth downloads each feed's newest again at its next check, or the next time it opens." : {
      "comment" : "After Cancel stops feed downloads that the newest-N rule downloads again by itself."
    },
    "TextMouth exports one spoken audio file at a time. Export this once the current one has finished." : {
      "comment" : "Why a spoken audio export was refused: another one is running."
    },
    "TextMouth first saves a copy of the old file, and does not rebuild if it cannot." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of what Rebuild Library Index does when no copy has been saved yet: it saves one first."
    },
    "TextMouth found no braille tables in its bundle." : {
      "comment" : "Shown in the Braille tab of Settings in place of the pop-ups when the app holds no braille tables."
    },
    "TextMouth has no braille table named “%@”." : {
      "comment" : "Why a braille translation was refused: no braille table has this name. %@ is the table's name as liblouis or macOS gives it."
    },
    "TextMouth has no rules of its own: none was right in every book tested. Edit Rules… opens your copy, where you can add rules, such as a name the recognizer always spells another way." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Clean Up Transcript sheet when the rules that come with the app are empty. Edit Rules… is the name of a button of the sheet."
    },
    "TextMouth hasn't merged it or removed it." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the report of a conflicting copy: nothing was done with it. \"It\" is the copy."
    },
    "TextMouth hasn't read the latest save yet." : {
      "comment" : "Reason after a colon: a rebuild left the book's text alone because the latest save of the edited text is not read yet."
    },
    "TextMouth hasn't read this book's headings yet. Open the book once, then export again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book's headings could not be exported, after the file's name in a failure sentence such as \"Couldn't export Headings: ...\"."
    },
    "TextMouth is already moving its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an operation was refused: the library is already being moved."
    },
    "TextMouth is already transcribing %@. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when a transcription is started while another runs. %@ is the title of the audiobook being transcribed."
    },
    "TextMouth is also open on “%@” (active %lld minutes ago)." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the warning that another Mac has this library open. %1$@ is that Mac's name; %2$lld is how many minutes ago it was last active.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth is also open on “%@” (active %lld minute ago)."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth is also open on “%@” (active %lld minutes ago)."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is also open on “%@” (active less than a minute ago)." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the warning that another Mac has this library open. %@ is that Mac's name."
    },
    "TextMouth is finishing up before it quits: %@. It quits when that is done." : {
      "comment" : "Panel text and announcement while TextMouth finishes work before quitting. %@ is the list of what is under way, such as \"saving the library and keeping downloads\", already joined in the language's own list style."
    },
    "TextMouth is getting them now, and the library opens when they arrive." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why the library can't be used yet: the files are being fetched from the cloud, and the library opens by itself when they arrive. \"Them\" means the library's files named in the sentence before."
    },
    "TextMouth is moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an operation was refused: books are being moved between folders."
    },
    "TextMouth is moving books between folders. Wait until that finishes, then choose %@ again." : {
      "comment" : "Why Replace Existing waits: TextMouth is moving books between folders. %@ is the name of the Replace Existing button, which the sentence asks the user to choose again."
    },
    "TextMouth is not downloading right now." : {
      "comment" : "Why the download of a feed's next episode did not start: the app is quitting or the feed is being deleted. Said after \"The next episode could not be downloaded, so playback stopped.\"",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "TextMouth no está descargando en este momento."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth is opening again on another library, so they stay unsaved in this one." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save stays unsaved: TextMouth is switching to another library. \"They\" is the changes that could not be saved."
    },
    "TextMouth is opening again on another library, so they stay where they are in this one." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files stays undone: TextMouth is switching to another library. \"They\" is the files."
    },
    "TextMouth is quitting and the book's audio doesn't hold these edits yet. Discard undoes them; next time you edit this book, Redo brings them back until you make another edit. Cancel keeps TextMouth open." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the question about the audio editor's unsaved edits asked as TextMouth quits: what Discard and Cancel do."
    },
    "TextMouth is reading the library's text again. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why a book can't be read again while the library's text is being read again (the launch batch, Redo Text Extraction), in the words TextMouth uses while its storage work is held (StorageBusyError)."
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again in another encoding. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again in another encoding, in the same words as extractionRefusal: a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with another braille code. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with another braille code, as the other re-reads' sentences say it (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:), BrailleFileCodeWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth is reading “%@” again with other braille file characters. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. Why what would rewrite the text of the braille book titled bookTitle waits while TextMouth reads it again with other braille file characters, as the encoding's sentence says it for any other book (TextEncodingWording.readingAgainRefusal(bookTitle:)): a second re-read of it, Edit Text, Redo Text Extraction, and Replace Existing (LibraryViewModel.readingAgainRefusal(of:)). Placeholders in order: bookTitle."
    },
    "TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why an operation was refused: the library is being rebuilt."
    },
    "TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory. Wait until that finishes, then choose %@ again." : {
      "comment" : "Why Replace Existing waits: TextMouth is rebuilding its data directory, the folder that holds the library. %@ is the name of the Replace Existing button, which the sentence asks the user to choose again."
    },
    "TextMouth is replacing “%@” with the new copy. Try again when that finishes." : {
      "comment" : "Why an action on a book is refused while Replace Existing makes the new copy ready, such as Edit Text or opening the book. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "TextMouth is still carrying out your last answer. Wait until it finishes." : {
      "comment" : "What an import question says when it is answered again while the previous answer is still being carried out."
    },
    "TextMouth is still saving them." : {
      "comment" : "The reason that ends \"Changes to the feed “Planet Money” could not be saved:\" in the quit prompt and banner. Them are the feed's changes."
    },
    "TextMouth is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: TextMouth kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path."
    },
    "TextMouth is switching to another library and opening again on it." : {
      "comment" : "Why an operation was refused: TextMouth is switching to another library."
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to make changes in %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the chosen location can't be used: macOS does not let TextMouth write there. %@ is the folder's path."
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to post notifications. Turn them on in System Settings, Notifications, TextMouth." : {
      "comment" : "What the notifications setting's help says while macOS does not allow TextMouth to post notifications. System Settings and Notifications are macOS's own names, in the language of macOS."
    },
    "TextMouth isn't allowed to use the microphone. Turn it on in System Settings, Privacy & Security, Microphone." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when macOS has denied TextMouth the microphone. Names the places in System Settings, as macOS words them, where the user can allow it."
    },
    "TextMouth keeps the original file of audio it converts at import. An original takes about as much disk space as its converted file, or twice as much when uncompressed. Export offers it as the Original file. A feed episode's original is not kept: it can be downloaded again." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the Keep Originals switch while it is on. \"Original file\" names the choice Export offers; keep it the same as that choice's translation."
    },
    "TextMouth kept the text you changed in %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the message when an automatic rebuild left a book's edited text alone. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "TextMouth left it there and is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish, when one item appeared: TextMouth left the item and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path.\nSecond sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: TextMouth left what was put there and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path."
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which hold no sound it can read." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out several files that hold no sound TextMouth can read. %@ is the files' count and names, such as \"2 files, “a.spx” and “b.spx”\"."
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which holds no sound it can read." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out one file that holds no sound TextMouth can read. %@ is the file's name in curly quotes."
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which need TextMouth's converter, missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out several files that only TextMouth's own converter reads, because the converter is missing from the app. %@ is the files' count and names, such as \"2 files, “a.avi” and “b.wmv”\". Advice to install the app again follows."
    },
    "TextMouth left out %@, which needs TextMouth's converter, missing from the app." : {
      "comment" : "Notice that a book left out one file that only TextMouth's own converter reads, because the converter is missing from the app. %@ is the file's name in curly quotes. Advice to install the app again follows."
    },
    "TextMouth left them there and is still using %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish, when several items appeared: TextMouth left the items and kept using the current data directory. %@ is the current data directory's path."
    },
    "TextMouth makes a folder named after the feed in %@, and its episodes and articles download into it." : {
      "comment" : "The line under the folder picker of the Add Feed sheet. %@ is the library folder chosen, or the name of the library's top level."
    },
    "TextMouth makes a new library index from the books in this folder." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before opening the library without its index file."
    },
    "TextMouth moved %@ to the current library format, but with a problem:" : {
      "comment" : "Lead-in of the alert about one book that moved into the current library format with a problem. %@ is a count of books, such as \"1 book\". The book's line follows."
    },
    "TextMouth moved %@ to the current library format, but with problems:" : {
      "comment" : "Lead-in of the alert about several books that moved into the current library format with problems. %@ is a count of books, such as \"3 books\". The books' lines follow."
    },
    "TextMouth moved %lld new copies of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copies of four or more duplicate books to the Trash, because their questions were never answered. %lld is the number of books. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth moved %lld new copy of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth moved %lld new copies of duplicate books to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth moved the new copies of %@ to the Trash, because the questions whether to keep them as duplicates were never answered before TextMouth closed. To get them back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copies of two or three duplicate books to the Trash, because their questions were never answered. %@ is their titles in curly quotes, listed as a sentence lists them. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash."
    },
    "TextMouth moved the new copy of “%@” to the Trash, because the question whether to keep it as a duplicate was never answered before TextMouth closed. To get it back, open the Trash and choose Put Back." : {
      "comment" : "Alert after the launch moved the new copy of one duplicate book to the Trash, because its question was never answered. %@ is the book's title. \"Put Back\" is Finder's command in the Trash."
    },
    "TextMouth moves them back once it has finished moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files waits: it runs when books have been moved between folders. \"Them\" is the files."
    },
    "TextMouth moves them back once it has finished rebuilding its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files waits: it runs when the data directory has been rebuilt. \"Them\" is the files."
    },
    "TextMouth moves them back once the move of its data directory ends." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed move of files waits: it runs when the move of the data directory ends. \"Them\" is the files."
    },
    "TextMouth needs the drive “%@” connected to open the library." : {
      "comment" : "What using a library on another drive means. %@ is the drive's name."
    },
    "TextMouth opens the book's manifest.json in your text editor." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the Edit Manifest explanation. manifest.json is a file name and stays as written."
    },
    "TextMouth opens the book's text in your text editor, as a Markdown file." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the Edit Text explanation. Markdown is the name of a text format."
    },
    "TextMouth reads BRF and BRL files you add from now on with these characters, and recognizes Unicode braille patterns by itself. The Export dialog starts a BRF with them. A book keeps its import characters, which Book Information can change." : {
      "comment" : "The caption under the braille file characters pop-up in the Braille tab of Settings. BRF and BRL are braille file formats, and Book Information is a window."
    },
    "TextMouth reads braille files (BRF, BRL, and PEF) with this code and exports with it unless the Export dialog chooses another. A book keeps the code it was imported with." : {
      "comment" : "The caption under the code pop-ups in the Braille tab of Settings. BRF, BRL, and PEF are braille file formats."
    },
    "TextMouth reads its file as it reads a file you add: in the encoding the file names, or else the one TextMouth finds." : {
      "comment" : "Text of Speak Info, Book Information's braille code and text encoding rows, and the re-read alerts. What Automatic does, as the alert says it before it is chosen."
    },
    "TextMouth saves them once it has finished moving books between folders." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save waits: it runs when books have been moved between folders. \"Them\" is the changes that could not be saved."
    },
    "TextMouth saves them once it has finished rebuilding its data directory." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save waits: it runs when the data directory has been rebuilt. \"Them\" is the changes that could not be saved."
    },
    "TextMouth saves them once the move of its data directory ends." : {
      "comment" : "Why a failed save waits: it runs when the move of the data directory ends. \"Them\" is the changes that could not be saved."
    },
    "TextMouth skipped %lld entries of “%@”: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after a playlist imported with entries left out. %1$lld is the number of entries skipped, %2$@ the playlist's name, and %3$@ the list of the entries, each with its reason in parentheses.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "TextMouth skipped %lld entry of “%@”: %@."
                }
