            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth stopped reading this document because %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a document was refused at import: the program that reads it ran too long or used too much memory and was stopped. %@ is the reason, a clause in English that follows \"because\"."
    },
    "TextMouth stopped the braille translation because %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a braille translation ended. %@ is the reason, a clause such as \"an earlier call was abandoned\", which stays English until the engine's sentences convert."
    },
    "TextMouth stops checking this feed for new articles." : {
      "comment" : "The first sentence of the confirmation before Unsubscribe, for a feed of articles."
    },
    "TextMouth stops checking this feed for new episodes." : {
      "comment" : "The first sentence of the confirmation before Unsubscribe, for a feed of episodes."
    },
    "TextMouth stops checking this feed for new items." : {
      "comment" : "The first sentence of the confirmation before Unsubscribe, for a feed of episodes and articles."
    },
    "TextMouth waited for it." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why the library can't open: TextMouth waited for the missing file to arrive. \"It\" is the file named in the sentence before."
    },
    "TextMouth will open the library in %@ instead of the one in %@, which isn't available." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before using another library while the one in use is not available. %1$@ is the chosen folder's path; %2$@ is the path of the library in use.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will open the library in %1$@ instead of the one in %2$@, which isn't available."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will open the library in %@ the next time it opens, but it couldn't open again by itself: %@" : {
      "comment" : "First part of the message when Use This Library could not open TextMouth again. %1$@ is the library's folder; %2$@ is the system's reason, a sentence.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will open the library in %1$@ the next time it opens, but it couldn't open again by itself: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will quit and open again to load it." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before using another library: TextMouth opens again."
    },
    "TextMouth will quit and open again to start it." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before starting a new library: TextMouth opens again."
    },
    "TextMouth will start a new, empty library in the default location, %@, instead of the library in %@, which isn't available." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before starting a new library. %1$@ is the default location's path; %2$@ is the path of the library in use, which is not available.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will start a new, empty library in the default location, %1$@, instead of the library in %2$@, which isn't available."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth will stop using the library in %@ (%@) and open the library in %@ instead." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before using another library. %1$@ is the path of the library in use; %2$@ is what it holds, such as \"743 books, 2 feeds\"; %3$@ is the chosen folder's path.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth will stop using the library in %1$@ (%2$@) and open the library in %3$@ instead."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth writes %@ with a new identity for the library, and opens it." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before giving the library a new identity file. %@ is the identity file's name, which stays as written."
    },
    "TextMouth writes %@ with the identity this Mac knows for the library, and opens it." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the question asked before restoring the library's identity file. %@ is the identity file's name, which stays as written."
    },
    "TextMouth's converter could not make itself safe before reading “%@”, so it did not read the file." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: TextMouth's converter could not confine itself before reading it, so it did not read the file. %@ is the file's name. Advice to install the app again follows."
    },
    "TextMouth's converter gave back audio of “%@” that TextMouth could not read." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: what TextMouth's converter gave back was not audio TextMouth reads, which only a damaged copy of the app could make. %@ is the file's name. Advice to install the app again follows."
    },
    "TextMouth's converter stopped before the end of “%@”, so it could not be imported." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: TextMouth's converter ended before the end of its sound, with no error. %@ is the file's name."
    },
    "TextMouth's converter stopped unexpectedly while reading “%@”. The file may be damaged." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was not imported: TextMouth's converter stopped unexpectedly while reading it, as a damaged file can make it do. %@ is the file's name."
    },
    "TextMouth's own filters don't include “%@”. They are %@; with ffmpeg installed, every filter it has works." : {
      "comment" : "Problem said of a filter TextMouth doesn't run itself. %1$@ is the filter's name as typed, and %2$@ the list of the filters TextMouth does run, such as \"a, b, and c\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "TextMouth's own filters don't include “%1$@”. They are %2$@; with ffmpeg installed, every filter it has works."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "TextMouth's own filters run this chain." : {
      "comment" : "Shown under a filter preset's chain field: every filter in it is one TextMouth runs itself."
    },
    "TextMouth's own loudnorm normalizes with one gain, so it takes only true" : {
      "comment" : "What the loudnorm filter's linear option accepts, said at the end of a refusal such as \"The loudnorm filter's linear can't be “false”: <this>.\" Written without its full stop."
    },
    "TextMouth's own rules are newer, version %@. To use them, delete your copy or copy their rules into it." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Clean Up Transcript sheet when the rules that come with the app are newer than the user's copy. %@ is the new version number, written without digit grouping."
    },
    "That OPML file is damaged at line %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: its markup is damaged. The first %@ is the line number of the fault, an identifier written without digit grouping. The second is a short technical reason in English, from the parser, kept English as detail for a bug report.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "That OPML file is damaged at line %1$@: %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That OPML file lists no feeds." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: it lists no feed TextMouth can subscribe to."
    },
    "That address isn't a web address TextMouth can open." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed could not be fetched: its address is not an http or https address."
    },
    "That file is empty." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: it is empty."
    },
    "That file isn't an OPML list of subscriptions." : {
      "comment" : "Why an OPML file of subscriptions could not be imported: it is another kind of file."
    },
    "That isn't a web address. Enter a feed's address, or the address of a page that names one." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe refused: the address typed is not a web address."
    },
    "That item isn't a plain file TextMouth can read." : {
      "comment" : "Alert explaining why a chosen item was not attached as a transcript: it is not an ordinary file, such as a folder or a pipe."
    },
    "That keeps the book's copy in the cloud." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of why Remove Download was refused: what the service's own command does."
    },
    "That match is no longer in the book's text. Search again to find it." : {
      "comment" : "Announcement when a search match is no longer in the book's text."
    },
    "That page doesn't name a feed." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe refused: the web page names no feed."
    },
    "That page names %lld feeds. Choose one, then Subscribe." : {
      "comment" : "What the Add Feed sheet says when a web page names several feeds. %lld is how many feeds the page names. Subscribe is the name of the Subscribe button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "That page names %lld feed. Choose one, then Subscribe."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "That page names %lld feeds. Choose one, then Subscribe."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "That would put %@ %lld levels deep, but folders nest at most %lld levels." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when a folder edit would nest a folder too deep. %1$@ is the folder's location, in straight double quotes. %2$lld is how many levels deep it would be. %3$lld is the most levels allowed.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
