          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original file was kept: it is a folder, and an import never deletes a folder." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after a book was imported from a folder, such as an RTFD: the original was kept because an import never deletes a folder."
    },
    "The original file will be moved to the Trash after a successful import." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in Storage settings under the choice that deletes the original file after an import, while files go to the Trash."
    },
    "The original file will be permanently deleted after a successful import." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in Storage settings under the choice that deletes the original file after an import, while files are deleted permanently."
    },
    "The original file will remain untouched after import." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in Storage settings when the original file is kept after an import."
    },
    "The original file you imported is not changed." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the warning shown under the metadata editor's switch while it is on: the file the user first imported stays as it was."
    },
    "The original file you imported is not touched." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the hint of the metadata editor's switch that also writes the EPUB file: the file the user first imported stays as it was."
    },
    "The original file “%@” could not be deleted: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Alert about the original file of an imported book that could not be deleted. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$@ the reason, a sentence of the system's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The original file “%1$@” could not be deleted: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original file “%@” could not be moved to the Trash: %@" : {
      "comment" : "Alert about the original file of an imported book that could not be moved to the Trash. %1$@ is the file's name and %2$@ the reason, a sentence of the system's.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "The original file “%1$@” could not be moved to the Trash: %2$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "The original is the lossless take a recording is saved from, or a copy of an audiobook's file from before its first edit. Keeping it lets every edit be undone without loss; a recording's costs about 345 MB an hour. A change also applies to originals already kept, and in a cloud library an original syncs with its book." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the Original audio picker in Storage settings (Audio Editing): what an original is, what keeping it costs (345 MB is for an hour of a recording), and that a change reaches originals already kept."
    },
    "The page at %@ is larger than TextMouth reads." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed article's download failed: the web page is too large. %@ is the server's host name."
    },
    "The part of the book chosen has no words to speak." : {
      "comment" : "Why a spoken audio export was refused: the chosen part of the book has no words."
    },
    "The pauses couldn't be found." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor couldn't find the audio's pauses. A sentence giving the reason follows."
    },
    "The place, bookmarks, and transcript kept for it are deleted too." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of the confirmation before a feed's episode or article is deleted: what TextMouth kept of the listener's for it goes too."
    },
    "The playlist “%@” is not a complete, valid playlist file." : {
      "comment" : "Refusal of an XSPF playlist that is not a readable XML playlist. %@ is the playlist's file name."
    },
    "The playlist “%@” uses XML entities of its own, which TextMouth does not read." : {
      "comment" : "Refusal of an XSPF playlist that declares XML entities of its own. %@ is the playlist's file name."
    },
    "The podcast directory at %@ couldn't answer the search (error %@). Try again later." : {
      "comment" : "Why a podcast search failed: the directory answered with an error. The first %@ is the server's host name; the second is the error's number, an identifier written without digit grouping, such as 503.",
      "localizations" : {
