                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "There isn't enough free space to download %lld reading list books"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "There isn't room on this Mac for this episode (%@)." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed's episode could not be downloaded: the disk is too full. %@ is the file's size with its unit, such as 61 MB."
    },
    "There isn’t enough free space on the disk." : {
      "comment" : "Why an import failed when the disk is full. Said instead of the system's own sentence, which names a hidden internal file."
    },
    "There's an empty filter between two commas." : {
      "comment" : "Problem found in a typed filter chain (the audio editor's Apply Filter and the filter presets): two commas in a row leave a filter with nothing in it."
    },
    "There's no audio after the cursor to preview." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the audio editor has no audio after the cursor to preview a filter on."
    },
    "There's no feed at that address any more." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed could not be fetched: the address answers that nothing is there (error 404)."
    },
    "There's no library in %@ to use, and none to move there while the library isn't available." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why the chosen folder can't be used: it holds no library and there is none to move. %@ is the folder's path."
    },
    "There's nothing to redo." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the audio editor's Redo when nothing has been undone."
    },
    "There's nothing to undo." : {
      "comment" : "Said when Undo is asked for and there is no edit to undo, and the hint of a dimmed Undo in the audio editor."
    },
    "These books could not be deleted and remain in the library:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading over the books that could not be deleted permanently, several of them. One line for each book follows."
    },
    "These books could not be moved to the Trash and remain in the library:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading over the books that could not be moved to the Trash, several of them. One line for each book follows."
    },
    "These books could not be removed from the library and remain in it:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the error alert's list when Remove from Library Only could not mark the packages of several books, so they stay in the library. Each book's title and the reason follow on their own lines.\nHeading over the books that could not be removed from the library, several of them. One line for each book follows."
    },
    "These books were removed from the library, but their bookInfo.json files could not be deleted. They stay out of the library:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the error alert's list when Remove from Library Only removed several books but could not delete the bookInfo.json files in their packages. bookInfo.json is a file name. Each book's title and the reason follow on their own lines."
    },
    "These edits need the original audio, which is no longer kept." : {
      "comment" : "Said when the edits wait to be rendered from an original audio that is gone. A second sentence says what helps."
    },
    "These items could not be deleted and remain in the library:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading over the items of a folder that could not be deleted permanently, several of them. One line for each follows."
    },
    "These items could not be moved to the Trash and remain in the library:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading over the items of a folder that could not be moved to the Trash, several of them. One line for each follows."
    },
    "These items could not be removed from the library and remain in it:" : {
      "comment" : "Heading over the items of a folder that could not be removed from the library, several of them. One line for each follows."
    },
    "These transcript files beside the audio weren't attached: %@. The debug log says why." : {
      "comment" : "Notice after an import: several transcript files found beside the audio were not attached. %@ is their names as a list, such as \"“03.vtt”, “07.vtt”, and “09.srt”\"."
    },
    "They are listed after the differences." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the results of Compare Libraries that follows the count of unread files: the files are listed after the differences."
    },
    "They stay in %@" : {
      "comment" : "Announcement after Remove Download removed several books' files from this Mac: the books are still in the cloud. %@ is the cloud service's name, or \"the cloud\" when it is unknown."
    },
    "This Feed Uses Plain http" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the warning shown once after subscribing to a feed whose address uses plain http, which is not encrypted. Title case."
    },
    "This Feed's Settings" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group of settings a feed can have of its own, in Feed Info. Title case."
    },
    "This Mac can't run the speech model that transcription uses." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when transcription is tried on a Mac whose hardware cannot run the speech model."
    },
    "This Mac doesn't allow TextMouth to use the microphone: a device management profile or Screen Time restricts it." : {
      "comment" : "Error in the Record window when something other than the user, a device management profile or Screen Time, keeps TextMouth from using the microphone."
    },
    "This Mac doesn't know the library's identity, so it can't restore it." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence of why the library can't open: this Mac has no record of the library's identity, so the identity file can't be restored from it."
    },
    "This Mac is offline, so %@ can't be refreshed. Connect to the internet and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed could not be refreshed: this Mac has no internet. %@ is the feed's title or server."
    },
    "This Mac is offline, so the book can't be downloaded from %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a book can't be downloaded: the Mac is offline. %@ is the cloud service's name, or \"the cloud service\" when it is unknown."
    },
    "This Mac is offline, so the directory can't be searched. Connect to the internet and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a podcast search failed: this Mac has no internet."
    },
    "This Mac is offline, so “%@” can't be downloaded. Connect to the internet and try again." : {
      "comment" : "Why a feed item's download failed: this Mac has no internet. %@ is the item's title."
    },
    "This Mac no longer has the chosen table, “%@”; choose another." : {
      "comment" : "Under the pop-ups in the Braille tab of Settings: the chosen braille table of this Mac is gone. %@ is the table's stored name, \"mac:\" and its file name."
    },
    "This Mac's braille table “%@” changed from liblouis %@ to %@ since the book was read, so TextMouth keeps the book's text as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book is not read with its braille table again: the table changed. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it, %2$@ the liblouis version the book was read with, and %3$@ the version now.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "This Mac's braille table “%1$@” changed from liblouis %2$@ to %3$@ since the book was read, so TextMouth keeps the book's text as it was."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This Mac's braille table “%@” may have changed since liblouis %@ read the book, so TextMouth keeps the book's text as it was." : {
      "comment" : "Why a book is not read with its braille table again: the table may have changed. %1$@ is the table's name as macOS gives it and %2$@ the liblouis version the book was read with.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "This Mac's braille table “%1$@” may have changed since liblouis %2$@ read the book, so TextMouth keeps the book's text as it was."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "This Window" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the Open the next book in pop-up button (Settings, Playback; Feed Info; Folder Settings): the next book opens in the window already open, in place of the book there.",
