    },
    "Times" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the group in Playback settings that holds the setting about naming the speed beside times."
    },
    "Title" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the audio editor's field for a chapter marker's title.\nLabel of the field in the Record window that names the recording, which becomes the audiobook's title.\nName of a way to sort the books: by the title. Shown in the Sort menu, the library view editor, the window title, and in sort announcements.\nName of the book information sheet's field for the book's title.\nText of the Library window's View pop-up and Go to View. The one item of the Sort menu of a view listing only feeds, which are always listed by title."
    },
    "Title for a chapter marker at the cursor. One already there is renamed." : {
      "comment" : "Explains the title field of the audio editor's Insert Chapter Marker sheet."
    },
    "Title or Author" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A kind of test as a condition's test pop-up names it. This is the case .titleOrAuthorContains."
    },
    "Title:" : {
      "comment" : "Caption beside the title field of the New Book from Text sheet. VoiceOver skips it; the field has its own label."
    },
    "Titles" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the Library settings section that holds the Leading Articles pop-up, which decides how book titles are sorted and typed."
    },
    "Titles sort, and are found by typing, as they are written: The Hobbit is among the T's." : {
      "comment" : "Describes the Leading Articles choice Part of the Title, under the pop-up. The Hobbit is the example title; the T's are the books sorted under the letter T."
    },
    "To" : {
      "comment" : "The label of the pop-up in the Export dialog's spoken audio options that chooses where the spoken audio ends."
    },
    "To %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line of the move sheet that says where the library is going. %@ is the new location's path."
    },
    "To download it again, choose %@ on its row." : {
      "comment" : "After Cancel stops one feed download that only the listener's Download brings back. %@ is the name of the Download command."
    },
    "To download the other %lld again, choose %@ on their rows." : {
      "comment" : "After Cancel stops feed downloads, the rest of which only the listener's Download brings back. The first %lld is how many; %@ is the name of the Download command.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "To download the other %lld again, choose %@ on its row."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "To download the other %lld again, choose %@ on their rows."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "To download the other one again, choose %@ on its row." : {
      "comment" : "After Cancel stops feed downloads, the one other of which only the listener's Download brings back. %@ is the name of the Download command."
    },
    "To download them again, choose %@ on their rows." : {
      "comment" : "After Cancel stops several feed downloads that only the listener's Download brings back. %@ is the name of the Download command."
    },
    "To free the space anyway, choose Show in Finder, then %@." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of why Remove Download was refused: how to free the space by hand. Show in Finder is a command's name. %@ is a clause that tells what to do in the cloud service's own app, such as \"choose Remove Download\"."
    },
    "To keep an article, choose %@ on its row first." : {
      "comment" : "The last sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, for a feed of articles. %@ is the name of the Move to Library command."
    },
    "To keep an episode, choose %@ on its row first." : {
      "comment" : "The last sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, for a feed of episodes. %@ is the name of the Move to Library command."
    },
    "To keep an item, choose %@ on its row first." : {
      "comment" : "The last sentence of the confirmation before Delete Feed, for a feed of episodes and articles. %@ is the name of the Move to Library command."
    },
    "To let it go, take it off the reading list, or clear %@ in the Reading List's options." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of why Stop Keeping on This Mac cannot let a book go: the reading list keeps it. %@ is the name of the Reading List's option that keeps its books downloaded, as the option shows it."
    },
    "To let them go, take them off the reading list, or clear %@ in the Reading List's options." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of why Stop Keeping on This Mac cannot let several books go: the reading list keeps them. %@ is the name of the Reading List's option that keeps its books downloaded, as the option shows it."
    },
    "To the default location, %@" : {
      "comment" : "Line of the move sheet that says where the library is going: the default location. %@ is its path."
    },
    "To use another folder, open Settings, Storage, and choose %@ or %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence on the Library Not Available screen that points to the way to another library. Settings and Storage are the names of the settings window and its tab; %1$@ and %2$@ are the names of two buttons in Storage settings, as they show them.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "To use another folder, open Settings, Storage, and choose %1$@ or %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "To use it, choose %@ on the Text tab in Settings." : {
      "comment" : "Advice after the refusal of a pronunciation lexicon on the Mac. %@ is the title of the import button on the Text tab of Settings, which is another string of the app."
    },
    "To use it, open the book and choose %@ from the Book menu." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of a notice after an import, saying how to attach the transcript file by hand. %@ is the name of the Attach Transcript command in the Book menu."
    },
    "Together with the archives inside it, the archive expands to %@, more than the %@ TextMouth extracts from archives holding audio or other archives." : {
      "comment" : "Why an import's archive was refused when it holds other archives. %1$@ is the total size they expand to, such as \"2 GB\"; %2$@ is the limit for archives that hold audio or other archives.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Together with the archives inside it, the archive expands to %1$@, more than the %2$@ TextMouth extracts from archives holding audio or other archives."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Together with the archives inside it, the archive expands to %@, more than the %@ TextMouth extracts from archives without audio." : {
      "comment" : "Why an import's archive was refused when it holds other archives. %1$@ is the total size they expand to, such as \"2 GB\"; %2$@ is the limit for archives that hold no audio.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Together with the archives inside it, the archive expands to %1$@, more than the %2$@ TextMouth extracts from archives without audio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Together with the archives inside it, the archive holds %@ files and folders, more than the %@ TextMouth extracts in one import." : {
      "comment" : "Why an import's archive was refused when it holds other archives. %1$@ is how many files and folders they hold in all, already formatted; %2$@ is the limit, already formatted.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Together with the archives inside it, the archive holds %1$@ files and folders, more than the %2$@ TextMouth extracts in one import."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Toggle Bookmark" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Bookmarks group and read by VoiceOver. Adds a bookmark at the reading position, or removes the one there. Also the title of the menu command of the same name."
    },
    "Too long to keep for pasting. To move it, paste right after cutting." : {
      "comment" : "Said by the audio editor's Paste when the audio cut was too long to keep for pasting."
    },
    "Too many timed passages: the limit is %lld." : {
      "comment" : "Error shown when a chosen transcript file holds more timed passages than the app reads. %lld is the limit, written with the region's digit grouping.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
