                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "Unread: %@ wasn't read, because TextMouth stopped waiting after %lld seconds in all, %@"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Unreadable file" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the path of the unreadable library index file, on the library index recovery sheet."
    },
    "Unsubscribe" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the command that stops checking a feed when it acts at once, and of the confirmation's button. Title case."
    },
    "Unsubscribe from %@?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the confirmation before Unsubscribe. %@ is the feed's title."
    },
    "Unsubscribed" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the first case of the condition.\nThe note after a feed's title while the listener is unsubscribed from it, so TextMouth does not check it. Title case."
    },
    "Unsubscribed from %@: TextMouth no longer checks it for new articles%@." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says once Unsubscribe is done, for a feed of articles. The first %@ is the feed's title; the second is a clause about the downloads that stay, which may be empty.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Unsubscribed from %1$@: TextMouth no longer checks it for new articles%2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Unsubscribed from %@: TextMouth no longer checks it for new episodes%@." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says once Unsubscribe is done, for a feed of episodes. The first %@ is the feed's title; the second is a clause about the downloads that stay, which may be empty.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Unsubscribed from %1$@: TextMouth no longer checks it for new episodes%2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Unsubscribed from %@: TextMouth no longer checks it for new items%@." : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver says once Unsubscribe is done, for a feed of episodes and articles. The first %@ is the feed's title; the second is a clause about the downloads that stay, which may be empty.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Unsubscribed from %1$@: TextMouth no longer checks it for new items%2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Unsubscribe…" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the command that stops checking a feed, when it asks first because it would delete places and bookmarks kept for removed downloads. The ellipsis says a question follows. Title case."
    },
    "Unsupported file format: .%@" : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was refused at import: TextMouth does not read its format. %@ is the file's extension without its dot. No advice follows."
    },
    "Unsupported file format: .%@." : {
      "comment" : "Why a file was refused at import: TextMouth does not read its format. %@ is the file's extension without its dot. Advice on what to do follows."
    },
    "Until then, changing the location and rebuilding the directory are unavailable." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the Storage settings explanation while the library index can't be read."
    },
    "Untitled" : {
      "comment" : "The name given to an exported file or folder, or to an entry of an exported EPUB, when the book's title or the heading has no words."
    },
    "Untitled rule" : {
      "comment" : "The name a substitution rule is given in lists and announcements when it has neither a name nor a pattern."
    },
    "Up Arrow" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a key of the keyboard, spoken by VoiceOver and shown in braille in a keyboard shortcut such as \"Command + Up Arrow\"."
    },
    "Up One Level" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Navigation group and read by VoiceOver. Goes up one level, to the folder that holds the current one.\nToolbar button of a Library window that goes up to the folder that holds the folder shown."
    },
    "Updates the default voice, speed, and pitch for every book without settings of its own." : {
      "comment" : "Hint and tooltip of the buttons that save a text book's voice, speed and pitch as the settings for every book."
    },
    "Updating text cache" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the progress shown while TextMouth brings every book's text cache up to date."
    },
    "Use %@ and %@, or drag, to reorder. Rules apply top to bottom." : {
      "comment" : "Help in the footer of the Substitutions settings on reordering rules. %1$@ and %2$@ are the titles of the Move Up and Move Down commands, which stay as those commands show them.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Use %1$@ and %2$@, or drag, to reorder. Rules apply top to bottom."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Use Default Location..." : {
      "comment" : "Button in Storage settings, shown while the library isn't available, that opens the library in the default location or starts a new one there. The three dots show that a question follows."
    },
    "Use Global Default" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the book's own settings sheet that removes its own end of book choice, so the setting for every book applies."
    },
    "Use Regex" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the switch in Search in Book that makes the search text a regular expression. Regex is short for regular expression."
    },
    "Use This Library" : {
      "comment" : "Button of the question that confirms using the library the chosen folder holds."
    },
    "Use This Library?" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the question asked before using the library the chosen folder holds."
    },
    "Use ffmpeg for filters" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the switch in Storage settings (Audio Editing) that lets the audio editor's filters run through an installed ffmpeg program. ffmpeg is the program's name."
    },
    "Use it after parser updates." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the caption under the Redo Text Extraction button in Storage settings. \"It\" is Redo Text Extraction."
    },
    "Use regular expression" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Use Regex switch in Search in Book."
    },
    "Use regular expression matching" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Regular expression switch in the substitution rule editor."
    },
    "Use the default location" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver label of the Use Default Location button in Storage settings."
    },
    "Use the global setting (%@)" : {
      "comment" : "A choice of the Open the next book in pop-up button in Feed Info and Folder Settings: do as Settings says. %@ is the name of the choice Settings has now, such as This Window.\nThe first choice of the Audio Info pop-up for a book's original audio: follow the global setting. %@ is that setting's name, such as \"Keep\".\nTitle of the checkbox that makes a feed follow the global setting. %@ is the global setting's value, such as \"Every item listed, newest 5 downloaded\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
