    "When Applicable" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). A visibility as the Visibility pop-up names it: \"Always\", \"When Applicable\", or \"Hidden\". This is the case .whenApplicable."
    },
    "When New Episodes Arrive" : {
      "comment" : "Heading of the third group of the Feeds tab of Settings: alerts and notifications. Title case."
    },
    "When a book ends" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the Reading List's options bar pop-up button choosing what a book opened from the list does when it ends: play the book below, play the book above, or stop.",
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Al terminar un libro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "When a book is deleted, %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the explanation in Storage settings of what removing a book does. %@ says what happens to the book's files, such as \"its files go to the Trash, where you can recover them until the Trash is emptied\"."
    },
    "When articles are ignored, a book whose metadata names French, German, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Dutch, Catalan, Swedish, Danish, or Norwegian passes over that language's articles, such as Le and Die, and The." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the note under the Leading Articles pop-up, shown where articles are ignored. Names the languages whose articles TextMouth skips; Le, Die, and The are example articles and stay as written."
    },
    "When book ends" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the pop-up in the Playback settings that chooses what happens when a book ends."
    },
    "When checked, matches must use the same upper and lower case" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Match Case checkbox."
    },
    "When checked, the search text is an ICU regular expression" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Regular Expression checkbox in the Search Library window. ICU is the name of the regular expression syntax, and stays as written."
    },
    "When checked, this feed follows the setting in Settings, %@; uncheck it to give the feed its own" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the checkbox that makes a feed follow the global setting. %@ is the name of the Feeds tab of Settings."
    },
    "When enabled, playback starts automatically after jumping to a heading, bookmark, or search result" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Auto-play after navigation checkbox in the Playback settings."
    },
    "When enabled, search text is treated as a regular expression" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Use Regex switch in Search in Book."
    },
    "When enabled, use \\b in the pattern for word boundaries" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Regular expression switch in the substitution rule editor. \\b is regular expression syntax and stays as written."
    },
    "When off, its files are deleted permanently and cannot be recovered." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the hint of the setting that moves deleted files to the Trash: what happens with the setting off."
    },
    "When off, removing a book will %@ at once." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of the hint of the setting that confirms before removing a book. %@ is what deleting does, such as \"move the files to the Trash\"."
    },
    "When off, the sheet stays open showing the remaining time and a reset button" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Close sheet after setting timer checkbox in the Playback settings."
    },
    "When on, a braille file read as contracted Unified English Braille that is clearly English Braille, American Edition is read as that instead." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the guess switch in the Braille tab of Settings. Unified English Braille and English Braille, American Edition are the names of braille codes."
    },
    "When on, a deleted book's files go to the Trash, where you can recover them until the Trash is emptied." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the hint of the setting that moves deleted files to the Trash: what happens with the setting on."
    },
    "When on, removing a book first asks whether to %@ or keep them in the TextMouth library folder." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the hint of the setting that confirms before removing a book. %@ is what deleting does, such as \"move the files to the Trash\"."
    },
    "When resuming playback, rewind to the start of this unit" : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint of the Rewind to pop-up in the Playback settings."
    },
    "When this book ends" : {
      "comment" : "Title of the book's own settings menu that chooses what happens when this book ends."
    },
    "When you save, TextMouth checks the manifest and rearranges the book, keeping your place in its track." : {
      "comment" : "Fourth sentence of the Edit Manifest explanation: what happens when the user saves the manifest."
    },
    "When you save, the book updates and keeps your place as near as it can." : {
      "comment" : "Fourth sentence of the Edit Text explanation: what happens when the user saves the edited text."
    },
    "Where Am I?" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Information group and read by VoiceOver. Speaks a short summary of the reading position. Also the title of the menu command of the same name.\nName of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the audio editor group and read by VoiceOver. Speaks the position and the selection.\nTitle of the reader toolbar's button that says where the reader is in the book."
    },
    "Where Am I? Announces current position in the book" : {
      "comment" : "What VoiceOver calls the reader toolbar's Where Am I? button while nothing is announced."
    },
    "Where Am I? Full Summary" : {
      "comment" : "Name of a keyboard shortcut action, listed in Settings in the Information group and read by VoiceOver. Speaks the full summary of the reading position. Also the title of the menu command of the same name."
    },
    "Where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs. %@ keeps them with your books, so they move and sync with the library. %@ keeps them in %@, which never syncs. A change applies from the next line; existing logs stay." : {
      "comment" : "VoiceOver hint and tooltip of the Log location pop-up in the Storage settings. %1$@ and %2$@ are the names of its two choices, as the pop-up lists them, and %3$@ is the folder's path on this Mac, which stays as written.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Where TextMouth writes its diagnostic logs. %1$@ keeps them with your books, so they move and sync with the library. %2$@ keeps them in %3$@, which never syncs. A change applies from the next line; existing logs stay."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Where none of their words are left, %@, each goes to about the same point in its chapter, or to the nearest passage the two readings share." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of what a re-read does to the listener's place and bookmarks. %@ is an example of when that happens, such as \"as when garbled letters become Cyrillic\", set between commas."
    },
    "Where none of their words are left, each goes to about the same point in its chapter, or to the nearest passage the two readings share." : {
      "comment" : "Second sentence of what a re-read does to the listener's place and bookmarks, without an example."
    },
    "Where the audio begins: the book's beginning, or a heading." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the From pop-up in the Export dialog's spoken audio options."
    },
    "Whether each page's last line carries its braille page number." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Braille page numbers switch in the Export dialog's braille options."
    },
    "Whether that code's braille is contracted, which writes common words and letter groups in fewer cells." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the contraction pop-up in the Braille tab of Settings."
    },
    "Whether that code's braille is contracted." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the contraction pop-up in the Export dialog's braille options."
    },
    "Which track of %@ do you want to edit?" : {
      "comment" : "Question asked before editing a book of several audio tracks. %@ is the book's title."
    },
    "While TextMouth was copying its data, %@ was changed to lead to %@ instead of %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: the new location's link was changed while the data was copied. %1$@ is the link's path; %2$@ is where it leads now; %3$@ is where it led before.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "While TextMouth was copying its data, %1$@ was changed to lead to %2$@ instead of %3$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "While TextMouth was copying its data, %lld items appeared in %@: %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: items appeared in the new location while the data was copied. %1$lld is how many; %2$@ is the new location's path; %3$@ is their names as a list.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "variations" : {
            "plural" : {
              "one" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "While TextMouth was copying its data, %lld item appeared in %@: %@."
                }
              },
              "other" : {
                "stringUnit" : {
                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "While TextMouth was copying its data, %lld items appeared in %@: %@."
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "While TextMouth was copying its data, something else was put at %@." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of why a move of the data directory did not finish: something else was put at the new location while the data was copied. %@ is the new location's path."
    },
    "Whole File" : {
      "comment" : "Choice in the audio editor's Apply Filter sheet: filter all of the audio."
    },
    "Whole word only" : {
      "comment" : "A part of a substitution rule's spoken summary: the rule matches whole words only."
    },
    "Windows Media" : {
      "comment" : "The name of the Windows Media container format, as people say it. Inside sentences about importing a file of that format."
    },
    "With \"%@\", Play on a finished book says it is finished; with \"%@\", Play starts it again from the beginning." : {
      "comment" : "Caption under the When book ends picker in Settings, Playback. %1$@ and %2$@ are the names of two of the picker's choices, as the picker shows them (Stop, and Stop, and Play Starts Over); Play is the reader's Play button.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "With \"%1$@\", Play on a finished book says it is finished; with \"%2$@\", Play starts it again from the beginning."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Con “%1$@”, Play en un libro terminado avisa que ya está terminado; con “%2$@”, Play lo vuelve a empezar desde el principio."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With %@, %@." : {
      "comment" : "A sentence that explains one button of a removal question. %1$@ is the button's title, such as \"Move to Trash\", and %2$@ says what it does, such as \"its files go to the Trash, where you can recover them until the Trash is emptied\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "With %1$@, %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With %@, the feed and its downloads stay, listed in no folder until Feed Info gives the feed another; Delete Feed… on its row deletes it." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder that holds one feed's folder. %@ is the title of the button that deletes everything, such as \"Move Everything to Trash\". \"Feed Info\" and \"Delete Feed…\" name a sheet and a command."
    },
    "With %@, the feeds and their downloads stay, listed in no folder until Feed Info gives each another; Delete Feed… on a feed's row deletes it." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder that holds several feeds' folders. %@ is the title of the button that deletes everything, such as \"Move Everything to Trash\". \"Feed Info\" and \"Delete Feed…\" name a sheet and a command."
    },
    "With %@, the folder and everything in it leave the library, and %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder. %1$@ is the title of its button that deletes everything, such as \"Move Everything to Trash\", and %2$@ says what happens to the files, such as \"their files go to the Trash, where you can recover them until the Trash is emptied\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "With %1$@, the folder and everything in it leave the library, and %2$@."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "With Move Contents Out, the feed's folder moves with the rest." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder that holds one feed's folder. \"Move Contents Out\" is the name of one of its buttons."
    },
    "With Move Contents Out, their folders move with the rest." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder that holds several feeds' folders. \"Move Contents Out\" is the name of one of its buttons."
    },
    "With Move Contents Out, they stay in the library and only the folder is deleted." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the dialog that asks how to delete a folder. \"Move Contents Out\" is the name of one of its buttons."
    },
    "Within the Last" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library view editor sheet, which makes and changes a view of the Library window, and of the descriptions of a view's filter. A condition's relation as its relation pop-up names it, by its test and whether it is negated. This is the form for the other case of the condition."
    },
    "Word 2003 XML" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book format of a Word 2003 XML document, shown in a book's information, the format column, and the duplicate finder."
    },
    "Word 97-2003 Document" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book format of an old Microsoft Word document (.doc), from Word 97 to 2003, shown in a book's information, the format column, and the duplicate finder."
    },
    "Word 97-2003 document. Its headings are plain text, so Word's navigation pane omits them." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Convert to picker in the Export dialog while Word 97-2003 is chosen. Word is an app's name."
    },
    "Word Count" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's row that shows how many words the book has."
    },
    "Word Document" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book format of a Microsoft Word document (.docx), shown in a book's information, the format column, and the duplicate finder."
    },
    "Word count" : {
      "comment" : "Label of a book's number of words in its read-only Book Information sheet."
    },
    "Words per minute" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the voice sheet's speed slider, shown beside it.\nTitle of the default speed slider in the Voice settings."
    },
    "Works in" : {
      "comment" : "Label of the pop-up button in a keyboard shortcut action's row that chooses in which windows the shortcut works, such as every window or Library windows."
    },
    "Works in %@" : {
      "comment" : "Says where a keyboard shortcut works, in a row of the Shortcuts tab or an announcement. %@ names the windows, such as \"every window\", \"Library windows\", or \"the audio editor\"."
    },
    "Writes chapter markers and markers beside the audio, in an Audacity label file of the same name." : {
      "comment" : "Hint of the Also write the markers as Audacity labels checkbox. Audacity is the name of an audio editing program."
    },
    "Writes the title, author, publisher, and date into the library's copy of this book." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of the hint of the metadata editor's switch that also writes the EPUB file."
    },
    "Writes this and every other too-deeply nested chapter of this export as plain paragraphs of lines, without asking again." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Export Every Such Chapter as Written button in the alert an export shows when a chapter nests too deeply."
    },
    "Writes this chapter as plain paragraphs of its lines, and exports everything else as usual." : {
      "comment" : "The hint of the Export as Written button in the alert an export shows when a chapter nests too deeply."
    },
    "Year" : {
      "comment" : "Name of the book information sheet's field for an audiobook's year; VoiceOver reads it as the field's label."
    },
    "You can make a new folder here." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the message of the folder chooser that Change Location opens: the chooser has a button that makes a folder."
    },
    "You can open and read books, and reading positions are still saved with each book, but changes to the library itself are not saved until you choose one of the options below." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the library index recovery sheet: what still works, and what does not until an option is chosen."
    },
    "You can recover it from the Trash until the Trash is emptied." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the confirmation about the original file of a book just imported, and the hint of its Move to Trash button: the file can be recovered from the Trash."
    },
    "You cleaned it up on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of Book Information's Transcript detail saying when the user cleaned up the transcript. %@ is a date, such as \"October 5, 2026\"."
    },
    "You cleaned up this transcript on %@. Transcribing again replaces the cleanup." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Transcribe Audio sheet warning that transcribing again replaces the cleanup the user applied. %@ is a date, such as \"October 5, 2026\"."
    },
    "You edited it on %@." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of Book Information's Transcript detail saying when the user edited the transcript. %@ is a date, such as \"October 5, 2026\"."
    },
    "You edited the transcript on %@, after the cleanup. Undo Cleanup undoes those edits too." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Clean Up Transcript sheet warning that undoing the cleanup also undoes the user's later edits. %@ is a date, such as \"October 5, 2026\". Undo Cleanup is the name of a button of the sheet."
    },
    "You edited this transcript on %@. Transcribing again replaces your edits." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Transcribe Audio sheet warning that transcribing again replaces the user's own edits. %@ is a date, such as \"October 5, 2026\"."
    },
    "You will be asked whether to delete the original file permanently after each import." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in Storage settings under the choice that asks about the original file after each import, while files are deleted permanently."
    },
    "You will be asked whether to move the original file to the Trash after each import." : {
      "comment" : "Caption in Storage settings under the choice that asks about the original file after each import, while files go to the Trash."
    },
    "You're already subscribed to %@." : {
      "comment" : "Why Subscribe refused: the feed is already in the library. %@ is the feed's title."
    },
    "Your books and reading positions are kept." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the Rebuild Directory confirmation."
    },
    "Your copy of the rules is empty. Edit Rules… opens it to add some." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Clean Up Transcript sheet when the user's own rules file holds no rule. Edit Rules… is the name of a button of the sheet."
    },
    "Your copy of the rules is only in the cloud, so TextMouth asked for it and uses its own meanwhile." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Clean Up Transcript sheet when the user's own rules file has not been downloaded from the cloud drive yet."
    },
    "Your edited text was also kept as %@, in the book's package." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence saying where a backup of the user's edited text was kept. %@ is a file name such as content.md.edited-20261004T123012Z, which stays as written."
    },
    "Your edits to the transcript are deleted too." : {
      "comment" : "Last sentence of the question asked before a transcript is deleted, when the user had edited it."
    },
    "Your edits to the transcript are replaced too." : {
      "comment" : "Sentence of the question asked before a transcript from a file replaces the book's, when the user had edited it."
    },
    "Your library (%@) will upload to %@ in the background." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of what moving the library into a cloud folder means. %1$@ is the library's size, such as \"5.5 GB\"; %2$@ is the cloud service's name.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "Your library (%1$@) will upload to %2$@ in the background."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Your library is empty. Add to Library adds a book." : {
      "comment" : "The only row of an empty library. \"Add to Library\" is the name of the button that adds a book, so keep it the same as that button's label."
    },
    "Your library will upload to %@ in the background." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of what moving the library into a cloud folder means, when its size is not known. %@ is the cloud service's name."
    },
    "Your place and bookmarks move with their words." : {
      "comment" : "First sentence of what a re-read does to the listener's place and bookmarks."
    },
    "Your rules file can't be used: %@. TextMouth keeps it and a copy, and uses its own rules until you correct it." : {
      "comment" : "Line of the Clean Up Transcript sheet when the user's own rules file is damaged. %@ is the reason, a short technical phrase in English."
    },
    "a book that is not in the library" : {
      "comment" : "What Compare Libraries calls a Reading List book that neither copy's library holds, in lower case, inside a sentence."
    },
    "a book's record, %@" : {
      "comment" : "A phrase naming a book's record file inside a sentence about a conflicting copy. %@ is the file's name, which stays as written."
    },
    "a feed's index of its episodes, %@" : {
      "comment" : "A phrase naming a feed's index file inside a sentence about a conflicting copy. %@ is the file's name, which stays as written."
    },
    "a feed's record, %@" : {
      "comment" : "A phrase naming a feed's record file inside a sentence about a conflicting copy. %@ is the file's name, which stays as written."
    },
    "a folder no longer in the library" : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: the name a folder condition gives a folder that is no longer in the library, inside a filter's description such as \"folder is a folder no longer in the library\"."
    },
    "a kind the system does not name" : {
      "comment" : "Stands for the system's description of a kind of picture it has no description for, inside parentheses: \"TextMouth can't read this kind of picture (a kind the system does not name).\""
    },
    "a menu command has one shortcut" : {
      "comment" : "The reason, said after \"not recorded\", why a second key cannot be added to a menu command's shortcut. Lower case, since it follows a colon."
    },
    "a menu command's shortcut is one press of a key with Command or Control" : {
      "comment" : "The reason, said after \"not recorded\", why a keyboard shortcut cannot be a menu command's or a button's: it must be one press of a key held with Command or Control. Lower case, since it follows a colon."
    },
    "a package of its name is in both its library folder and its feed's" : {
      "comment" : "Why a downloaded feed item could not be moved between its feed's folder and the library: its files are in both folders. Lower case, without a full stop."
    },
    "about %@" : {
      "comment" : "A time estimate, said after \"Time to transcribe:\" or inside a sentence. %@ is a length of time in words, such as \"6 minutes\" or \"1 hour, 5 minutes\".\nPart of a checkbox's label in the Export dialog for text whose size is only close. %@ is a size such as 12 KB."
    },
    "about 140 MB" : {
      "comment" : "The approximate size of one language's speech model, said in the Download button's label. MB means megabytes."
    },
    "added last" : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: how a view's limit chooses rows, in lower case inside a filter's description: the items added most recently."
