                  "value" : "all %lld files"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "always" : {
      "comment" : "A Library view's visibility in lower case, inside a row's spoken label: the View pop-up always offers the view."
    },
    "another Mac" : {
      "comment" : "What the warning that TextMouth is open on another Mac calls that Mac when its name can't be read yet. It sits where the Mac's name would go, inside curly quotes, so it has no capital letter."
    },
    "articles" : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: the kind of row news articles, in lower case inside a filter's description such as \"Lists books and articles\"."
    },
    "as when garbled letters become Cyrillic" : {
      "comment" : "An example inside the sentence about what a re-read does to the listener's place: the places move when none of the old words are left, as when letters read wrongly become Cyrillic."
    },
    "at %@ of %@ at %@" : {
      "comment" : "Part of the text Copy Reading Position copies, for a text book. %1$@ is the time reached and %2$@ the book's length, both written as clock times such as 2:10:24; %3$@ is the reading speed they count at, such as \"500 words a minute\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
