                  "state" : "translated",
                  "value" : "at most %lld, %@"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "at once" : {
      "comment" : "The value of the days after playing that a download is deleted, when it is 0: the download is deleted as soon as it has played. Lower case."
    },
    "at the top of the library" : {
      "comment" : "Where a copy of the library files a book, inside a sentence of Compare Libraries: not in any folder."
    },
    "before page %@" : {
      "comment" : "Where the cursor is, said after \"the cursor is\": before the book's first page. %@ is the first page's label, an identifier written without digit grouping."
    },
    "bookmarks" : {
      "comment" : "The bookmarks that a deleted download or several kept, a noun inside a list such as \"the place and bookmarks kept for 1 removed download\". Lower case."
    },
    "books" : {
      "comment" : "Library view editor: the kind of row books, in lower case inside a filter's description such as \"Lists books and feeds\"."
    },
    "built in" : {
      "comment" : "Text of the Library tab of Settings, a list of the views the Library window offers (built-in views and the listener's own). The row's word for a view TextMouth made."
    },
    "by %@" : {
      "comment" : "Part of a book's spoken row label, after the title. %@ is the author's name, or Unknown.\nWho publishes a podcast, in the line under its title in the search results. %@ is the publisher's name."
    },
    "changes to books" : {
      "comment" : "What the saving failure of books' records is about, as a noun phrase inside a sentence, with no capital letter."
    },
    "chapter %@" : {
      "comment" : "A reading place inside a sentence of Compare Libraries. %@ is the chapter's number, an identifier written without digit grouping."
    },
    "chapter %@, %lld%%" : {
      "comment" : "A reading place inside a sentence of Compare Libraries. %1$@ is the chapter's number, an identifier written without digit grouping, and %2$lld is how far into the book it is, a percentage from 0 to 100.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "chapter %1$@, %2$lld%%"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "chapter %@, saved %@, and %@" : {
      "comment" : "A record's place and bookmarks inside a sentence about a conflicting copy of a book's record. %1$@ is the chapter's number, an identifier written without digit grouping; %2$@ is the date and time the place was saved; %3$@ is a count of bookmarks, such as \"2 bookmarks\".",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "chapter %1$@, saved %2$@, and %3$@"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "chapter %@, with no note" : {
      "comment" : "A bookmark's place inside a sentence of Compare Libraries, when it has no note. %@ is the chapter's number, an identifier written without digit grouping."
    },
    "chapter %@, with the note “%@”" : {
      "comment" : "A bookmark's place and note inside a sentence of Compare Libraries. %1$@ is the chapter's number, an identifier written without digit grouping, and %2$@ is the note the listener wrote.",
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "chapter %1$@, with the note “%2$@”"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "checking its format" : {
      "comment" : "What an import was doing with a file when it stopped, as a phrase that follows the name of a book in the import overlay (\"“Moby Dick.epub”, checking its format\") and, capitalized by the app, starts a failure (\"Checking its format failed: ...\"). Starts with a lowercase letter and has no full stop."
    },
    "checking the package" : {
      "comment" : "What an import was doing with a file when it stopped, as a phrase that follows the name of a book in the import overlay (\"“Moby Dick.epub”, checking the package\") and, capitalized by the app, starts a failure (\"Checking the package failed: ...\"). Starts with a lowercase letter and has no full stop."
    },
    "choose %@ again" : {
      "comment" : "The next step after a refusal to delete a feed whose download is in use: \"Close it, then choose Delete Feed… again.\" %@ is the name of the Delete Feed command. Lower case, without a full stop, to follow \"then\"."
    },
    "choose Make online-only" : {
